ions fail before missing support; global uniqueness claims are refused, required unasserted attributes remain excluded, and permanent compromise forbids restoration.","scope":"Policy covers exact declared evidence classes, operating-point/population fields, unasserted identity attributes, validity/event vocabulary, no-composition, and permanent template-breach rules."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:40ca87c06813e807b8cafc7ca447f08c6b99e47bc0ebd575a6ec6bad8c61cd14","reason":"They enforce exact evidence-class, population, unasserted-attribute, no-composition, template-irreversibility, trust-root, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The caller selects policy, trust-root labels, evidence, population, and clocks; neither labels nor signatures establish voluntary consent, personhood, witness independence, or institutional authority.","exceptions":"Only exact admitted evidence classes, vocabulary, finite bounds, and declared exclusions are accepted; no label, arrangement strength, or restorative event overrides HUMAN boundaries.","revisions":"Changed mechanism bytes, policy/request version, trust roots, HUMAN record, population, operating point, event log, or collection produces a different digest-bound selection."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:40ca87c06813e807b8cafc7ca447f08c6b99e47bc0ebd575a6ec6bad8c61cd14","reason":"They enforce exact evidence-class, population, unasserted-attribute, no-composition, template-irreversibility, trust-root, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Certificates bind exact requests, policies, mechanism/proposition digests, retained payload references, bounded evaluation, and explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED exclusions.","enforcement_points":"evaluate and native certificate recheck paths reject malformed or contradictory declarations and keep unavailable personhood/liveness/closure claims at UNKNOWN.","unavailable_behavior":"The HUMAN checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:40ca87c06813e807b8cafc7ca447f08c6b99e47bc0ebd575a6ec6bad8c61cd14","reason":"They enforce exact evidence-class, population, unasserted-attribute, no-composition, template-irreversibility, trust-root, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Represented participants are the declared subject, evidence/witness records, assertion or template declarant, and verifier; none is authenticated as a living person by these checks.","roles":"The HUMAN lifecycle and template checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"Declared states include unenrolled, active, withdrawn, dead, template-enrolled, compromised, and revoked, plus arrangement states that must never manufacture HUMAN.","transitions":"Enrollment, reverification, compromise, revocation, death, and permanent template-breach rules define the admitted retained transitions."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:40ca87c06813e807b8c