ent inventories, attributions, independent witness records/keys, mechanism pins, trust roots, and finite limits.","defaults":"The ACTOR checkers fails closed to UNKNOWN or FAIL when necessary selected evidence, support, compatibility, or bounded checking capacity is absent; it never infers approval from silence.","precedence":"Typed and commitment contradictions fail first; an actor cannot delegate to itself or beyond its classes, controlled/self witnesses do not establish accountability, and every selected decision must be attributed.","scope":"Policy covers declared control surfaces, instrument separation, admitted decision classes/spaces, delegation subsets and intervals, witness-key admission, succession, dissolution, and closure inventory."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"They enforce control-surface separation, decision classes, delegation scope, witness independence/key admission, attribution completeness, and fail-closed closure rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The checker admits configured witness keys and caller-selected ACTOR records; signatures prove key use only, not actor personhood, witness independence, legal authority, or consent.","exceptions":"Only exact declared delegation subsets, intervals, admitted spaces, event kinds, and independently admitted witness keys are considered; no implicit authority expansion is allowed.","revisions":"Changed control surface, decision class, admitted space, key set, event/decision record, policy, trust root, or mechanism bytes is a new digest-bound decision coordinate."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"They enforce control-surface separation, decision classes, delegation scope, witness independence/key admission, attribution completeness, and fail-closed closure rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Results bind exact ACTOR/collection bytes, selected decision/event/attribution inventories, witness signatures where available, requests, policies, and explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED boundaries.","enforcement_points":"Actor evaluate, closure, retention, replay, and recheck paths refuse invalid delegation/attribution/order and preserve unavailable independence or real-world completeness as UNKNOWN.","unavailable_behavior":"The ACTOR checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"They enforce control-surface separation, decision classes, delegation scope, witness independence/key admission, attribution completeness, and fail-closed closure rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Participants represented are the accountable actor, delegates, successors, instruments, independent witness-key holders, and verifier; actor and witness identities remain declared.","roles":"The ACTOR decision and accountability checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"States include active actor/key/decision-class sets, live or revoked delegations, membership, rotated keys, dissolved actors, succession pairs, and retained decision attribution/closure.","transitions":"Delegation, revocation, key rotation, membership entry/leave, dissolution, succession, decision attribution, and witness attestation define retained transitions."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"ACTOR sources define delegation, revocation, rotation, membership, dissolution, succession, decision-retention, attribution, and witness state/ordering replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact ACTOR typed records, control/instrument boundaries, decision-class vocabularies, semantic versions, canonical bytes, and installed mechanism digests define compatibility.","message_authority":"Admitted Ed25519 witness keys can bind exact decision statements and control-surface keys delimit declared actor control; neither proves real-world identity or independent custody.","ordering":"Event and decision positions are contiguous or strictly increasing, delegation intervals are ordered, succession ending/beginning pair at one position, and earlier decision records cannot be rewritten.","replay":"The ACTOR decision and accountability checks replays exact retained bytes and commitments; replay establishes consistency only and never repeats or proves a live-world event."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"ACTOR sources define delegation, revocation, rotation, membership, dissolution, succession, decision-retention, attribution, and witness state/ordering replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The ACTOR decision and accountability checks assumes retained inputs may be absent, malformed, stale, contradictory, unauthenticated, incomplete, or beyond finite checking bounds.","liveness":"No delegate, witness, successor, decision, or accountability response is guaranteed to appear; missing independent support remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"Recovery is deterministic replay of the selected base state, ordered events, retained decisions/attributions, and exact certificates; it performs no live authority restoration.","safety":"The checks reject self-delegation, out-of-class authority, instrument/actor overlap, conflicting succession, unattributed decisions, and witness keys within the actor's declared control surface."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d54598eba14fabc22dcf397ee6db6210d113cdbaf93508229a0c7b6603aa064e","reason":"ACTOR sources define delegation, revocation, rotation, membership, dissolution, succession, decision-retention, attribution, and witness state/ordering replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"The ACTOR verifier retains ROBOT.actuators as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative APPLIES while its owned closed-effect boundary is open. The concrete mechanism value and any external occurrence remain NOT_ESTABLISHED.","agent":"The ACTOR verifier retains ROBOT.agent as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative APPLIES while its owned closed-effect boundary is open. The concrete mechanism value and any external occurrence remain NOT_ESTABLISHED.","controllers":"The ACTOR verifier retains ROBOT.controllers as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.