he concrete mechanism value and any external occurrence remain NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"The sole authored reasons.vstd conservatively selects APPLIES for vstd-collective as MEASUREMENT so every MEASUREMENT obligation remains required while the owned closed-effect boundary is open. This obligation-retention decision is distinct from source-role evidence and establishes neither a concrete mechanism, authority, external effect, occurrence, checker PASS, nor Tier-1-plus fulfillment. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Inputs are exact COLLECTIVE and ROLE records, membership/charter/quorum commitments, endpoint certificates, decision inventories, assembly protocol, mechanism/trust selections, and bounds.","defaults":"The COLLECTIVE checkers fails closed to UNKNOWN or FAIL when necessary selected evidence, support, compatibility, or bounded checking capacity is absent; it never infers approval from silence.","precedence":"Membership and frozen charter/quorum consistency precede assembly; distinct selected members must meet feasible quorum and every decision-class requirement/countersign edge.","scope":"Policy covers selected membership, role graph, charter, quorum, assembly requirements, required/countersign roles, separation flags, decision classes, and admission/departure rules."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"They enforce charter, membership, quorum, required-role, countersign, separation, assembly, and fail-closed decision rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The caller selects charter, membership, quorum, roles, and child evidence; no source establishes legal existence, actual role occupancy, consent, or authority of the collective.","exceptions":"Only explicit selected separation flags, required roles, countersign edges, and admitted lifecycle actions are accepted; undeclared components cannot inflate quorum.","revisions":"Any changed member, charter, quorum, decision class, assembly rule, lifecycle endpoint, mechanism, or trust selection requires a new bound policy coordinate."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"They enforce charter, membership, quorum, required-role, countersign, separation, assembly, and fail-closed decision rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Certificates bind exact selected collections, membership/charter/quorum bytes, child replays, role and collective decision inventories, and explicit excluded claims.","enforcement_points":"Graph, decision, static-constraint, lifecycle, and closure evaluators reject inconsistent membership/assembly and keep absent real-world membership or actual decision execution unestablished.","unavailable_behavior":"The COLLECTIVE checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"They enforce charter, membership, quorum, required-role, countersign, separation, assembly, and fail-closed decision rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Participants represented are one collective, its selected ROLE members, role bearers/actors through child records, countersign roles, charter declarant, and verifier.","roles":"The COLLECTIVE membership and point-decision checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"States include fixed or changing ROLE membership, admitted/departed members, frozen charter/quorum coordinates, role decisions, and assembled collective point decisions.","transitions":"ROLE admission and departure move between exact endpoint collections; retained role decisions assemble a collective decision only when quorum, required roles, and countersign edges are satisfied."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"COLLECTIVE sources implement finite ROLE admission/departure and point-decision assembly protocols with explicit membership, quorum, countersign, ordering, replay, and recovery boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact COLLECTIVE/ROLE namespace records, selected protocol and charter versions, child request/policy/certificate bytes, mechanism pins, and finite limits define compatibility.","message_authority":"Typed ROLE children, retained charter/quorum commitments, and selected child certificates bind declarations; they do not establish live membership, natural-person separation, or legal collective authority.","ordering":"Membership events have unique contiguous positions and declared chronology; role/collective decision positions are complete, unique, and constrained to the selected point/period.","replay":"The COLLECTIVE membership and point-decision checks replays exact retained bytes and commitments; replay establishes consistency only and never repeats or proves a live-world event."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"COLLECTIVE sources implement finite ROLE admission/departure and point-decision assembly protocols with explicit membership, quorum, countersign, ordering, replay, and recovery boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The COLLECTIVE membership and point-decision checks assumes retained inputs may be absent, malformed, stale, contradictory, unauthenticated, incomplete, or beyond finite checking bounds.","liveness":"No member admission, departure, quorum assembly, countersignature, or collective decision progress is guaranteed; incomplete support remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"Recovery replays exact endpoint certificates, role decisions, and collective assemblies from retained bytes; it does not restore live membership or execute a collective decision.","safety":"The checks reject undeclared roles, duplicate/reused components, infeasible quorum, missing required/countersign roles, changed frozen terms, and transitions that modify unrelated records."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db0d7b289535cfdca6f393be6bd8ef5fb630b34e2e0a8cfd39cea4520a502898","reason":"COLLECTIVE sources implement finite ROLE admission/departure and point-decision assembly protocols with explicit membership, quorum, countersign, ordering, replay, and recovery boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment r