uth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The caller selects policies and child evidence; replayed relationships bind declared tokens only and do not establish live occupancy, personhood, role legitimacy, or consent.","exceptions":"Only explicitly admitted bearer classes, transition pairs, permission/scope changes, occupancy intervals, and selected exclusion groups are recognized.","revisions":"Changed ROLE facets, bearer limits, lifecycle protocol, matrix, permissions, scopes, endpoints, mechanism, or trust roots require a distinct bound evaluation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:05cf411f0a308cad6b83ffc03ea1de268c60fa0fbc338107824851d57e1d1cc2","reason":"They enforce bearer-class, simultaneous-limit, permission, scope, lifecycle-transition, exclusivity, and decision-authority rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Results bind exact ROLE/collection bytes, selected matrices/protocols, child replays, timed occupancy and decision inventories, requests, policies, and exclusions.","enforcement_points":"ROLE facet, constraint, lifecycle, and closure paths reject invalid occupancy/authority declarations and keep actual occurrence, live occupancy, and real-world completeness NOT_ESTABLISHED.","unavailable_behavior":"The ROLE checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:05cf411f0a308cad6b83ffc03ea1de268c60fa0fbc338107824851d57e1d1cc2","reason":"They enforce bearer-class, simultaneous-limit, permission, scope, lifecycle-transition, exclusivity, and decision-authority rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Participants represented are one ROLE class/seat, HUMAN or BOT bearers, responsible ACTOR/HUMAN roots through selected identity relations, a COLLECTIVE, and verifier.","roles":"The ROLE lifecycle and occupancy checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"States include selected lifecycle state, empty or bounded occupied bearer set, taking/leaving/handover endpoints, permissions/scopes, and retained point decisions.","transitions":"Configured lifecycle state pairs govern permitted permission/scope changes and taking/leaving; take, leave, paired handover, and checkpoint events reproduce exact endpoint occupancy."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:05cf411f0a308cad6b83ffc03ea1de268c60fa0fbc338107824851d57e1d1cc2","reason":"ROLE sources implement finite lifecycle, take/leave/handover occupancy, endpoint, and point-decision replay with explicit states, order, safety, and recovery. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact ROLE/COLLECTIVE/IDENTITY/ACTOR typed records, lifecycle protocol/matrix versions, child request/policy/certificate bytes, and finite bounds define compatibility.","message_authority":"Selected IDENTITY/ACTOR/HUMAN relationships and ROLE permissions bind declared authority tokens; live bearer authenticity, occupancy, consent, and institutional authority remain unestablished.","ordering":"Occupancy and decision positions are contiguous, clocks and endpoints follow the selected order, handover is paired, and simultaneous bearer limits/exclusive groups constrain states.","replay":"The ROLE lifecycle and occupancy checks replays exact retained bytes and commitments; replay establishes consistency only and never repeats or proves a live-world event."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:05cf411f0a308cad6b83ffc03ea1de268c60fa0fbc338107824851d57e1d1cc2","reason":"ROLE sources implement finite lifecycle, take/leave/handover occupancy, endpoint, and point-decision replay with explicit states, order, safety, and recovery. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The ROLE lifecycle and occupancy checks assumes retained inputs may be absent, malformed, stale, contradictory, unauthenticated, incomplete, or beyond finite checking bounds.","liveness":"No bearer takes/leaves a seat and no decision occurs merely because a retained protocol is valid; missing endpoint or identity support remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"Recovery is exact endpoint, occupancy-event, identity-relation, and decision replay; it cannot restore a live bearer or real authority.","safety":"The checks reject inadmissible bearer classes, over-capacity occupancy, illegal state transitions, out-of-scope permissions, duplicate actor-role cells, and mutually exclusive shared occupancy."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:05cf411f0a308cad6b83ffc03ea1de268c60fa0fbc338107824851d57e1d1cc2","reason":"ROLE sources implement finite lifecycle, take/leave/handover occupancy, endpoint, and point-decision replay with explicit states, order, safety, and recovery. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"decla