bstitute for selected child replay.","scope":"Policy covers bearer class, ROLE binding, occupancy interval, assurance and disclosure, attribute scope, HUMAN/BOT and SIM restrictions, lifecycle vocabulary, presentation prerequisites, and finite replay limits."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"They enforce bearer-class, ROLE/scope, assurance/disclosure, HUMAN/BOT/SIM separation, lifecycle, presentation, trust-selection, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The caller selects issuer/trust labels, policy, clocks, child evidence, and retained records; signature verification demonstrates key use only, not issuer authenticity, legal authority, consent, or current occupancy.","exceptions":"Only exact admitted bearer classes, lifecycle events, presentation algorithms, scope relations, successor rules, and finite vocabularies are recognized; no implicit transfer or privilege widening is accepted.","revisions":"Changed bearer, ROLE, scope, assurance, issuer/key, lifecycle or presentation bytes, child certificate, trust roots, clock, policy, or mechanism creates a distinct digest-bound coordinate."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"They enforce bearer-class, ROLE/scope, assurance/disclosure, HUMAN/BOT/SIM separation, lifecycle, presentation, trust-selection, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Results bind exact selected records, commitments, event and presentation inventories, signatures/children where selected, requests, policies, finite bounds, and explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED exclusions.","enforcement_points":"Occupancy, scope, lifecycle, presentation, and certificate recheck paths reject malformed or contradictory retained relations. The exit probe appends only to an ephemeral local event copy and reports actual enforcement NOT_ESTABLISHED.","unavailable_behavior":"The IDENTITY checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"They enforce bearer-class, ROLE/scope, assurance/disclosure, HUMAN/BOT/SIM separation, lifecycle, presentation, trust-selection, and fail-closed admission rules. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Participants represented are one HUMAN or BOT bearer, one ROLE seat, declared issuers/authorities, presentation verifiers, a selected SIM for BOT occupancy, and the checker; their real identities and authority remain unestablished.","roles":"The IDENTITY occupancy, lifecycle, and presentation checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"States include enrolled, active, renewed, revoked, expired, terminated, compromised, and successor states for one immutable bearer-to-ROLE binding, plus retained presentations.","transitions":"Enrollment, renewal, revocation, expiry, termination, compromise, successor enrollment, and presentation association are the finite retained transitions; HUMAN and BOT scope restrictions remain distinct."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"IDENTITY sources implement finite bearer-to-ROLE occupancy, lifecycle, successor, presentation, ordering, signature-check, and retained replay state machines. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact IDENTITY/HUMAN/BOT/ROLE/SIM records, lifecycle and presentation schema versions, declared algorithms, trust-root selections, mechanism digests, and finite bounds define compatibility.","message_authority":"Selected authority evidence references, issuer labels, admitted keys, child certificates, and presentation signatures bind retained statements only; they do not establish issuer custody, personhood, consent, or external role authority.","ordering":"Event positions are contiguous, commitments form the selected chain, time is nondecreasing, enrollment begins the lifecycle, terminal events are prospective, and presentations bind eligible prior events under the declared clock.","replay":"The IDENTITY occupancy, lifecycle, and presentation checks replays exact retained bytes and commitments; replay establishes consistency only and never repeats or proves a live-world event."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"IDENTITY sources implement finite bearer-to-ROLE occupancy, lifecycle, successor, presentation, ordering, signature-check, and retained replay state machines. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The IDENTITY occupancy, lifecycle, and presentation checks assumes retained inputs may be absent, malformed, stale, contradictory, unauthenticated, incomplete, or beyond finite checking bounds.","liveness":"No enrollment, renewal, revocation, termination, presentation, issuer response, or live eligibility progress is guaranteed; missing selected support remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"Recovery is deterministic replay of exact retained binding, event, presentation, child-certificate, and commitment bytes. It restores no live identity, role occupancy, or authority.","safety":"The checks reject bare AGENT bearers, HUMAN simulation scope, cross-bearer or cross-role substitution, invalid lifecycle order, post-terminal renewal/presentation, and inconsistent scope or occupancy."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4a4c9f8322ad5cde9a6b212d233095a6f73f5f54516d47bacd9117b2b303a3a8","reason":"IDENTITY sources implement finite bearer-to-ROLE occupancy, lifecycle, successor, presentation, ordering, signature-check, and retained replay state machines. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a31f1704c96cb45352fad9d296c437851b634d11b25b8bfe56488676e98ae809","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-identity-3deb6abf2bdc; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a31f1704c96cb45352fad9d296c437851b634d11b25b8bfe56488676e98ae809","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-identity-3deb6abf2bdc; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.3-consequences-and-intervention":{"declaration":{"hazards":"NOT_ESTABLI