HARDWARE evidence.","source":"The selected retained HARDWARE evidence bytes and their exact request, policy, object, and collection commitments."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:175f17d595d58cf595a6fcbe0df73afc561090c26c6fd72ee27eb00cd872bcb5","reason":"The HARDWARE measurement and substrate contracts validate retained quantities and observations at declared coordinates; they must distinguish supplied records from live or physically calibrated measurements. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"The checker receives a complete selected evidence artifact; acquisition latency and original arrival time are not observed.","observation_time":"Retained hardware measurement times are bounded integer microseconds on the evidence-declared clock, not trusted wall time.","reference_frame":"Each value is relative to its named device, unit, declared clock, and selected evidence coordinate.","uncertainty":"Physical accuracy, calibration, sampling error, clock truth, and device authenticity remain NOT_ESTABLISHED rather than being assigned zero uncertainty.","units":"Supported capacity units are bytes or dimensionless slots; contract-specific observed quantities retain their declared typed interpretation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:175f17d595d58cf595a6fcbe0df73afc561090c26c6fd72ee27eb00cd872bcb5","reason":"The HARDWARE measurement and substrate contracts validate retained quantities and observations at declared coordinates; they must distinguish supplied records from live or physically calibrated measurements. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"Freshness means current selected source and evidence commitments for this verification, not current physical-device state.","missingness":"Absent required evidence or unsupported interpretation yields UNKNOWN or refusal; missing values are never filled with zero.","provenance":"The certificate binds checker, request, policy, source, object, collection, and retained evidence digests without asserting who originally measured the value.","validity":"Canonical shape, exact commitments, supported identifiers and units, finite integer ranges, and contract-specific relations must all hold."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:175f17d595d58cf595a6fcbe0df73afc561090c26c6fd72ee27eb00cd872bcb5","reason":"The HARDWARE measurement and substrate contracts validate retained quantities and observations at declared coordinates; they must distinguish supplied records from live or physically calibrated measurements. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Exact request, policy, mechanism and evidence digests, selected object/collection, trust-root labels, and finite ceilings.","defaults":"Nothing is physically authenticated by default, and absent required evidence never becomes a passing empty record.","precedence":"Malformed or substituted bindings refuse before domain evaluation; bounded unavailability stays UNKNOWN; a reproduced contradiction is FAIL.","scope":"Admission of exact finite retained HARDWARE inventory, capacity, topology, measurement, and substrate claims."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2ab0e4bdcb1482c4b9314c887c0ff0b76a8a85739e31d157ca6bb438d545b7f5","reason":"Installed mechanism pins, trust-root labels, finite ceilings, and fail-closed verdict rules govern which retained HARDWARE claims these checkers will admit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The selected policy is activated for one verification call only and grants no allocation, spending, or physical-device authority.","authority":"The external caller selects policy and trust-root labels; this checker validates the selection but does not authenticate the real authority behind a label.","exceptions":"No bypass converts unsupported device kinds, units, bounds, or missing evidence into PASS.","revisions":"Installed mechanism and source digests bind the active rules; changed source or policy is a different selection."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2ab0e4bdcb1482c4b9314c887c0ff0b76a8a85739e31d157ca6bb438d545b7f5","reason":"Installed mechanism pins, trust-root labels, finite ceilings, and fail-closed verdict rules govern which retained HARDWARE claims these checkers will admit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unknown fields, stale digests, malformed records, and exhausted finite limits cannot silently reach the PASS path.","decision_evidence":"A bounded certificate records the selected proposition, bindings, outcome, and reproduced observations within the stated exclusions.","enforcement_points":"Request and policy parsing, mechanism/source binding, evidence bounds, namespace composition, and each domain relation check.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable physical truth, dependencies, or evidence remains UNKNOWN; the policy never treats it as absence or success."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2ab0e4bdcb1482c4b9314c887c0ff0b76a8a85739e31d157ca6bb438d545b7f5","reason":"Installed mechanism pins, trust-root labels, finite ceilings, and fail-closed verdict rules govern which retained HARDWARE claims these checkers will admit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declara