 are exact RECEIPT records and bytes, retained independent-audit fields, selected child certificates, prerequisite graph, chain anchors/items, issuer/key/signature selections, mechanism pins, and finite limits.","defaults":"The RECEIPT checkers fails closed to UNKNOWN or FAIL when necessary selected evidence, support, compatibility, or bounded checking capacity is absent; it never infers approval from silence.","precedence":"Canonical statics and digest commitments precede dependent replay; prerequisite and chain contradictions fail, signature validity cannot substitute for claim truth, and unavailable capacity or authority remains UNKNOWN.","scope":"Policy covers canonical VSTD-1 statics, selected audit replay, prerequisite closure, finite hash-chain continuity, admitted issuer-key signature checks, trust roots, and bounded evidence/certificate sizes."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"They enforce canonical encoding, digest and child selection, prerequisite/chain closure, admitted key/trust-root and signature rules, finite limits, and fail-closed exclusions. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy is activated only for one exact request, mechanism digest, trust-root selection, retained evidence coordinate, and finite limits; no ambient deployment is inferred.","authority":"The caller selects receipt bytes, issuer/key and trust-root labels, prerequisite children, chain anchors, and policy. Cryptographic validity proves use of an admitted key only, not authentic issuer identity, custody, governance, or authorization.","exceptions":"Only exact admitted schema versions, algorithms, trust-root selections, bounded child/cone/chain inventories, and canonical encodings are recognized; no label or successful replay promotes excluded claims.","revisions":"Changed receipt/audit bytes, prerequisite graph, chain anchor/tip, issuer/key/signature, installed checker TCB, trust roots, policy, or mechanism creates a distinct digest-bound decision."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"They enforce canonical encoding, digest and child selection, prerequisite/chain closure, admitted key/trust-root and signature rules, finite limits, and fail-closed exclusions. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Generic labels, declarations without selected support, stale bytes, foreign children, unregistered exceptions, and exhausted checks cannot be promoted to PASS.","decision_evidence":"Certificates bind exact selected records/bytes, request and policy digests, mechanism/TCB coordinates, retained children, chain/signature inputs, bounded outcomes, and exclusions.","enforcement_points":"Statics, validation replay, prerequisite closure, chain, authenticity, build, and native recheck paths reject malformed or contradictory retained evidence and preserve explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED fields.","unavailable_behavior":"The RECEIPT checkers preserves UNKNOWN for missing support or checking capacity and FAIL for retained contradictions; neither result authorizes downstream action."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"They enforce canonical encoding, digest and child selection, prerequisite/chain closure, admitted key/trust-root and signature rules, finite limits, and fail-closed exclusions. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Participants represented are one receipt subject, retained issuer/key labels, prerequisite receipt subjects, an audit producer, trust-root selector, and verifier; their real identity and authority remain unestablished.","roles":"The RECEIPT statics, replay, chain, authenticity, and closure checks assigns bounded declarant, subject, supporting-record, verifier, and transition roles; those labels do not authenticate real participants.","states":"States include canonical or malformed receipt bytes, audit replay PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN, prerequisite cone closure, chain genesis/tip continuity, signature-valid/invalid, and unsupported or unavailable evidence.","transitions":"The checks decode canonical statics, replay one retained audit, close selected prerequisites, advance a bounded hash chain, and validate an admitted issuer-key signature without generating or publishing a receipt."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"RECEIPT contracts implement canonical statics, deterministic audit replay, prerequisite-cone closure, bounded hash-chain ordering, issuer-key signature checking, and exact recovery/recheck protocols. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"VSTD-1 receipt models, canonical JSON/base64, certificate/request/policy schema versions, admitted signature algorithms, installed trusted-computing-base digest, mechanism pins, and finite bounds define compatibility.","message_authority":"Externally selected issuer ids, admitted public keys, trust-root labels, receipt signatures, and child certificates bind exact retained bytes only; key custody, issuer authenticity, governance, and authorization remain unestablished.","ordering":"Prerequisite edges must form the selected acyclic cone, receipt sequences are contiguous from the selected genesis, previous digests reach the exact tip, and audit replay binds one exact retained coordinate.","replay":"The RECEIPT statics, replay, chain, authenticity, and closure checks replays exact retained bytes and commitments; replay establishes consistency only and never repeats or proves a live-world event."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"RECEIPT contracts implement canonical statics, deterministic audit replay, prerequisite-cone closure, bounded hash-chain ordering, issuer-key signature checking, and exact recovery/recheck protocols. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The RECEIPT statics, replay, chain, authenticity, and closure checks assumes retained inputs may be absent, malformed, stale, contradictory, unauthenticated, incomplete, or beyond finite checking bounds.","liveness":"No receipt generation, issuer response, revocation publication, ledger registration, prerequisite availability, chain extension, or target rerun is guaranteed; unavailable evidence remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"Recovery rechecks exact retained receipt, audit, child-certificate, chain, and signature bytes. It does not regenerate an event, establish claim truth, reverse an action, or restore issuer authority.","safety":"The checks reject noncanonical bytes, digest substitution, prerequisite cycles or omissions, chain discontinuity, foreign children, signature mismatch, and replay disagreement within the selected bounds."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a4972f502aa3a358e03e5194fc68ce12ab83713a93100417691465384f1f88e7","reason":"RECEIPT contracts implement canonical statics, deterministic audit replay, prerequisite-cone closure, bounded hash-chain ordering, issuer-key signature checking, and exact recovery/recheck protocols. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8eb2d0c160404cf24d3e5210f8a2b02a757b4c88c706aa1fd8b8963a6fba36c4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-receipt-8d84ab1a897c; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8eb2d0c160404cf24d3e5210f8a2b02a757b4c88c706aa1fd8b8963a6fba36c4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-receipt-8d84ab1a897c; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.3-consequences-and-intervention":{"declaration":{"hazards":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","intervention":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","safe_state_or_continuity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8eb2d0c160404cf24d3e5210f8a2b02a757b4c88c706aa1fd8b8963a6fba36c4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-receipt-8d84ab1a897c; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.1-acquisition-and-observations":{"declaration":{"acquisition":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","deployment":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","measurements":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","phenomena":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8eb2d0c160404cf24d3e5210f8a2b02a757b4c88c706aa1fd8b8963a6fba36c4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-sensor-vstd-receipt-670260b3d76b; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.2-calibration-and-envelope":{"declaration":{"calibration_applicability":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","calibration_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","drift":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_range":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8eb2d0c160404cf24d3e5210f8a2b02a757b4c88c706aa1fd8b8963a6fba36c4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-sensor-vstd-receipt-670260b3d76b; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.3-sampling-and-faults":{"declaration":{"fault_dete