 collection, retained node/edge/order/closure bytes, endpoint commitments, child certificates, mechanism pins, and finite limits.","defaults":"Malformed, substituted, over-limit, unavailable, or contradictory input cannot default to PASS.","precedence":"Exact request and installed-policy checks precede evidence evaluation; order, closure, and lineage replay their selected GRAPH-3.1 child first.","scope":"Admission of exact retained GRAPH node/edge statics, least order, reachability closure, and direct operand-content lineage propositions."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:047ead5e5db2e8585f851d41ab96a52800bfb68737c843ad264715581f8fefc4","reason":"The package GRAPH graph_statics/order/closure/lineage _policy(), request, evaluation, build, and recheck paths enforce current mechanism pins, trust roots, finite bounds, child replay, and fail-closed retained-graph decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"A policy activates only when its exact version, mechanism identifier, current mechanism digest, trust roots, and certificate-byte ceiling are accepted.","authority":"The caller selects evidence and trust-root labels; the installed checker decides only its finite GRAPH proposition, not causal or lineage truth.","exceptions":"No implicit exception bypasses exact subject, collection, digest, child, or finite-limit equality.","revisions":"Schema, semantic, coordinate, mechanism, and source digests bind a revision; changed installed bytes require a new current mechanism digest."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:047ead5e5db2e8585f851d41ab96a52800bfb68737c843ad264715581f8fefc4","reason":"The package GRAPH graph_statics/order/closure/lineage _policy(), request, evaluation, build, and recheck paths enforce current mechanism pins, trust roots, finite bounds, child replay, and fail-closed retained-graph decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Undeclared edges, unsupported shapes, digest substitution, and skipped child replay are outside PASS rather than alternate admission paths.","decision_evidence":"Exact request, policy, retained evidence, child certificates, current source digest, and deterministic computed graph relations support the local verdict.","enforcement_points":"Each graph_*._policy(), request parser, bounded evaluator, certificate builder, and native recheck enforce the selected rule surface.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable evidence or exhausted bounded work remains unavailable or UNKNOWN; it is never promoted to a positive graph claim."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:047ead5e5db2e8585f851d41ab96a52800bfb68737c843ad264715581f8fefc4","reason":"The package GRAPH graph_statics/order/closure/lineage _policy(), request, evaluation, build, and recheck paths enforce current mechanism pins, trust roots, finite bounds, child replay, and fail-closed retained-graph decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","roles":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","transitions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1f84c0bc29ca7f15cf219ee4fdcb86432a9ad3df10cac48c994bd00ad929e76","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-protocol-vstd-package-graph-ed0490eca2a3; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","message_authority":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","ordering":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","replay":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1f84c0bc29ca7f15cf219ee4fdcb86432a9ad3df10cac48c994bd00ad929e76","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-protocol-vstd-package-graph-e