 checker policy.","authority":"The caller selects retained logical layout evidence; the checker has no host, device, allocator, storage, isolation, or data-movement authority.","exceptions":"There is no implicit exception to exact interval, extent, bijection, digest, child-replay, or finite-bound requirements.","revisions":"Version and installed source/mechanism digests identify the active checker; changed bytes require a newly bound policy."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a5f7d7f8ee26b4e1fd9f2ca8df5cab7f987e233214ef5c0d7322744c4bb83f78","reason":"SPACE layout/closure/migration _policy(), request, evaluation, build, and recheck paths enforce exact logical extents, child replay, current mechanism pins, trust roots, finite limits, and fail-closed outcomes. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unsupported or over-limit coordinates and child mismatches remain refusal or unavailability; they cannot be treated as physical allocation evidence.","decision_evidence":"Exact retained partition bytes, selected child certificates, migration rows, and current mechanism bytes support only the named logical proposition.","enforcement_points":"space_layout, space_closure, and space_migration policy parsers, request parsers, evaluators, builders, and rechecks enforce these rules.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable retained evidence remains UNKNOWN/unavailable and supplies no claim of allocation, copying, containment, isolation, or non-leakage."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a5f7d7f8ee26b4e1fd9f2ca8df5cab7f987e233214ef5c0d7322744c4bb83f78","reason":"SPACE layout/closure/migration _policy(), request, evaluation, build, and recheck paths enforce exact logical extents, child replay, current mechanism pins, trust roots, finite limits, and fail-closed outcomes. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; 