_estimate":"Counts and entropy are an exact census of selected retained rows, not an estimate of population prevalence, representativeness, or sampling-frame completeness.","phenomenon":"The exact canonical-value distribution of each selected field over the exact retained shard inventory.","source":"Exact caller-selected retained shard/record bytes bound to the DATA inventory; no live population or sensor acquisition is performed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:800875d7a0ebc6dc1c9560e73593a433e6be988456a9782271c6f44cd0eacb7d","reason":"data.distribution() derives exact canonical classes, counts, cardinality, and entropy_bits from the bound retained shard inventory under a selected 0..1e-9 bit tolerance, while excluding population, external-origin, and sensor claims. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"The checker reads retained evidence during evaluation but records no acquisition or arrival time for the underlying records.","observation_time":"The retained records carry no required observation timestamp in this mechanism; source or real-world observation time remains unestablished.","reference_frame":"The exact selected DATA object, complete retained shard inventory, sorted field name, and canonical JSON value representation.","uncertainty":"Selected counts are exact for retained bytes; entropy comparison allows only the explicit 0 through 1e-9 bit tolerance and models no sampling uncertainty.","units":"Class counts/cardinality and balance numerators/denominators are dimensionless; entropy and its tolerance are bits per retained observation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:800875d7a0ebc6dc1c9560e73593a433e6be988456a9782271c6f44cd0eacb7d","reason":"data.distribution() derives exact canonical classes, counts, cardinality, and entropy_bits from the bound retained shard inventory under a selected 0