s or explicit unavailable/refused/unknown outcome plus aggregate budget state.","saturation":"Unregistered, unavailable, refused, mismatched, over-limit, or nonreproducing replay is retained as FAIL or UNKNOWN and cannot be converted to an effect.","units_and_frames":"Exact bytes, dimensionless item/operation/member counts, finite Boolean assignments, route outcomes, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4425d4206ca4ddba2882b17d50f75fa9815f62698af030b195ce4fa0afa24496","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as ACTUATOR because verifier_coverage_closure.py dispatches exact installed DAG and boundary replay routes and observes their typed local effects before committing the aggregate result. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.3-feedback-and-interlocks":{"declaration":{"effect_feedback":"Response feedback is each registered route's reproduced computational status or explicit unavailable/refused/unknown outcome plus aggregate budget state.","failure_states":"Unregistered, unavailable, refused, mismatched, over-limit, or nonreproducing replay is retained as FAIL or UNKNOWN and cannot be converted to an effect.","interlocks":"Validate all request, policy, digest, and route bindings before dispatch; collect each bounded response before committing the aggregate certificate.","recovery":"Do not retry implicitly; repair the exact route or retained evidence and perform a separate fresh coverage evaluation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4425d4206ca4ddba2882b17d50f75fa9815f62698af030b195ce4fa0afa24496","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as ACTUATOR because verifier_coverage_closure.py dispatches exact installed DAG and boundary replay routes and observes their typed local effects before committing the aggregate result. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ASSET-0.1-identity-and-quantity":{"declaration":{"identity":"Exact artifact bytes, object and reason identifiers, source coordinates, digests, policies, receipts, and caller-selected retention paths.","precision":"Finite canonical bytes, items, operations, members, cases, evidence, registered routes, timeouts, selected algorithms, and source digests fail closed; the child subject's downstream effect envelope is not proven closed.","rights":"The caller may select and retain local verification artifacts only; no legal title, transferable property right, issuance, redemption, or financial claim is created.","units":"Exact bytes, artifact counts, record counts, and SHA-256 identities; no monetary quantity is represented."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e70c793690211c868b024aa6e5d951a0ed15105124b1c1240b47f619202ecf11","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as ASSET because it identifies and retains source, reason, certificate, report, and witness artifacts as digest-bound digital assets with explicit selection, retention, reconciliation, and non-property boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ASSET-0.2-issuance-and-redemption":{"declaration":{"backing_claims":"Asset applicability is limited to controlled digital evidence artifacts; it does not establish ownership, custody law, market value, backing, or redemption.","issuance_authority":"The caller may select and retain local verification artifacts only; no legal title, transferable property right, issuance, redemption, or financial claim is created.","redemption":"Preserve the prior digest, recapture or regenerate the exact artifact under a new identity, and reconcile references without claiming legal redemption.","supply_changes":"Create or retain a new local evidence artifact or receipt under explicit caller selection; source artifacts are never silently overwritten as proof."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e70c793690211c868b024aa6e5d951a0ed15105124b1c1240b47f619202ecf11","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as ASSET because it identifies and retains source, reason, certificate, report, and witness artifacts as digest-bound digital assets with explicit selection, retention, reconciliation, and non-property boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ASSET-0.3-custody-and-encumbrance":{"declaration":{"control":"Invoke installed finite verification or replay routes and, when explicitly selected, launch the named test or observer subject in a child process.","custody":"Digest-bound local source, reason, certificate, report, and witness artifacts at caller-selected paths under the current repository or output boundary.","encumbrances":"Malformed, contradictory, substituted, over-limit, or reproduced-negative evidence or child execution fails; missing, unsupported, unobservable, cancelled, timed-out, or unavailable evidence remains UNKNOWN and is never promoted to PASS.","reconciliation":"Selected identities and digests, parsed fields, proof and route outcomes, member and boundary counts, signature results, child return codes, coverage, audit events, explicit gaps, and typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN status."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e70c793690211c868b024aa6e5d951a0ed15105124b1c1240b47f619202ecf11","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as ASSET because it identifies and retains source, reason, certificate, report, and witness artifacts as digest-bound digital assets with explicit selection, retention, reconciliation, and non-property boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.1-feedback-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authority":"The exact VERIFIER-4.1 request and policy authorize only their finite local member and boundary replays; they grant no arbitrary process, physical, financial, release, or deployment authority.","commands":"Select and invoke only registered member and boundary replay routes, update the bounded aggregate state, and emit the resulting local decision.","feedback":"Feedback consists of DAG assessment state, each member's direct and qualified status, each boundary replay outcome, budget use, and explicit failure or unknown sets.","objectives":"Drive one bounded VERIFIER-4.1 evaluation toward the declared objective: every enumerated member and selected counterexample boundary must reach its required native replay state."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4425d4206ca4ddba2882b17d50f75fa9815f62698af030b195ce4fa0afa24496","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as CONTROLLER because verifier_coverage_closure.py uses member and boundary feedback to govern a bounded nonnested evaluation and select PASS, FAIL, or UNKNOWN under explicit operating limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.2-timing-and-stability":{"declaration":{"operating_envelope":"Finite members, nodes, boundary cases, artifact files, operations, items, evidence bytes, installed routes, and a nonreentrant local evaluation bound the control loop.","saturation":"Contradictory feedback produces FAIL; missing or unavailable feedback, budget exhaustion, unregistered routes, or absent cases produce UNKNOWN rather than an optimistic closure decision.","stability_assumptions":"VERIFIER finite coverage-closure controller controls a bounded software lifecycle, not a proved dynamical plant; safe downstream stability remains outside this Tier-0 claim.","timing":"Only source order, retained-event order, bounded operation counts, and explicit local completion are represented; no hard-real-time or eventual-progress guarantee is inferred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4425d4206ca4ddba2882b17d50f75fa9815f62698af030b195ce4fa0afa24496","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as CONTROLLER because verifier_coverage_closure.py uses member and boundary feedback to govern a bounded nonnested evaluation and select PASS, FAIL, or UNKNOWN under explicit operating limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.3-intervention-and-failure":{"declaration":{"arbitration":"Validate selection, policy, digests, limits, and evidence before native replay; aggregate explicit outcomes before certificate construction; recheck canonical bytes and source bindings before accepting a retained result.","failure_behavior":"Leave the prior result intact, restore a complete exact selection or available route, and start a fresh nonnested coverage evaluation.","feedback_loss":"Contradictory feedback produces FAIL; missing or unavailable feedback, budget exhaustion, unregistered routes, or absent cases produce UNKNOWN rather than an optimistic closure decision.","intervention":"Select and invoke only registered member and boundary replay routes, update the bounded aggregate state, and emit the resulting local decision."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4425d4206ca4ddba2882b17d50f75fa9815f62698af030b195ce4fa0afa24496","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as CONTROLLER because verifier_coverage_closure.py uses member and boundary feedback to govern a bounded nonnested evaluation and select PASS, FAIL, or UNKNOWN under explicit operating limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"FINBOT-0.1-agent-and-financial-authority":{"declaration":{"agent":"The selecting caller, witness runner, child subject, and any parties, accounts, venues, or services it reaches.","decision_scope":"Execute a caller-selected witness subject that may combine automated decisions with assets, accounts, markets, or financial effects; retain obligations because reach is not excluded.","financial_authority":"The verifier authorizes only local witness execution. It grants no account, asset, trading, payment, transfer, settlement, advisory, or fiduciary authority.","harness":"Strict bounded record validation, digest and signature binding, finite proof or route replay, explicit PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN aggregation, and canonical certificate reconstruction, plus explicit child-process witness execution."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as FINBOT because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose automated financial effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without asserting financial authority or occurrence. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"FINBOT-0.2-financial-exposure-and-dependencies":{"declaration":{"assets_and_parties":"The selected child subject and any financial parties, accounts, assets, venues, or endpoints it can reach.","exposure_limits":"Child timeout, exact subject identity, source digest, return code, coverage, and observer events bound the receipt; no exposure, position, loss, or transaction limit is enforced.","financial_dependencies":"SELECTED_CHILD_WITH_UNCLOSED_FINANCIAL_REACH; local execution is observed, but real-money, account, asset, market, payment, and settlement effects are not excluded.","real_world_paths":"The child may produce financial-agent effects outside the verifier's receipt; applicability retains the obligations without asserting that an effect occurred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as FINBOT because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose automated financial effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without asserting financial authority or occurrence. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"FINBOT-0.3-decisions-effects-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"decision_effect_evidence":"Child return code, named-subject coverage, declared observable audit events, stdout/stderr digests, and explicit missing or blind event classes.","intervention":"Launch only the named witness subject and record its outcome; no native order, payment, transfer, allocation, account, or settlement command is supplied.","limit_enforcement":"Strict bounded record validation, digest and signature binding, finite proof or route replay, explicit PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN aggregation, and canonical certificate reconstruction, plus explicit child-process witness execution.","reconciliation_and_recovery":"Preserve the receipt, stop at the child boundary, repair the witness or effect controls, and run a fresh observation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as FINBOT because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose automated financial effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without asserting financial authority or occurrence. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.1-authoritative-history":{"declaration":{"authority":"Only the caller-selected policy, installed route registry, and admitted trust roots authorize the named local verification step. No human, legal, physical, financial, publication, release, or deployment authority is created.","history":"Selected identities and digests, parsed fields, proof and route outcomes, member and boundary counts, signature results, child return codes, coverage, audit events, explicit gaps, and typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN status.","ordering":"Bind source and reason identities before execution, retain each child result before aggregation, and reconcile only against the same current coordinate.","state":"Prepared, running, HOLDS, REFUTED, UNKNOWN, failed, timed-out, stale-source, and reconciled entries remain distinct and append as new observations."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:6e92d50d9ba19e31b749b4a7cd11da7554ce2e97ca0006fad9589e97d533c851","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as LEDGER because the retained reasoning and integration sources preserve ordered gap, reason, witness, source-coordinate, and typed outcome records whose reconciliation and correction semantics must remain explicit. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.2-accounting-invariants":{"declaration":{"balance_rules":"verifier obligation and witness ledger is an ordered event/accounting ledger, not a fungible balance sheet. Its invariant is the exact authorized and ordered commit contract: Commit is one digest-bound local decision or witness receipt at its source coordinate; existing history is not rewritten into a stronger status.","rounding":"verifier obligation and witness ledger records exact discrete events and byte digests; it defines no numeric rounding convention or financial balance.","sources_and_sinks":"Append exact gap, decision, witness, and execution observations to the local run record; no financial balance or external settlement is represented.","units":"Ordered discrete entries, byte counts, exit codes, status counts, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:6e92d50d9ba19e31b749b4a7cd11da7554ce2e97ca0006fad9589e97d533c851","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as LEDGER because the retained reasoning and integration sources preserve ordered gap, reason, witness, source-coordinate, and typed outcome records whose reconciliation and correction semantics must remain explicit. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"verifier obligation and witness ledger does not rewrite an accepted history entry; later action is a new ordered event or a separately retained recovery operation.","reconciliation":"Selected identities and digests, parsed fields, proof and route outcomes, member and boundary counts, signature results, child return codes, coverage, audit events, explicit gaps, and typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN status.","recovery":"Preserve prior entries, repair the named source, reason, observer, or runner, then append a separately identified fresh execution and reconciliation.","replay":"A repeated call is a fresh evaluation of current bytes. Exact identities can detect substitution or duplicate selection but do not imply external idempotency."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:6e92d50d9ba19e31b749b4a7cd11da7554ce2e97ca0006fad9589e97d533c851","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as LEDGER because the retained reasoning and integration sources preserve ordered gap, reason, witness, source-coordinate, and typed outcome records whose reconciliation and correction semantics must remain explicit. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.1-orders-and-access":{"declaration":{"cancellation":"Stop at the bounded child result, preserve evidence, repair the selected witness, and rerun without retrying market effects.","order_states":"Selected, launched, running, observed, HOLDS, REFUTED, UNKNOWN, timed-out, and failed are verifier states; subject market states remain independently unestablished.","participant_access":"The verifier authorizes only local witness execution. It grants no trading, matching, allocation, pricing, settlement, account, or participant authority.","validation":"Strict bounded record validation, digest and signature binding, finite proof or route replay, explicit PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN aggregation, and canonical certificate reconstruction, plus explicit child-process witness execution."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as MARKET because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose market effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without claiming a native market or real trading authority. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.2-matching-and-allocation":{"declaration":{"allocation":"The child may produce market-like effects that the verifier does not prove confined; the retained verifier effect is execution plus bounded observation.","manipulation_controls":"Finite canonical bytes, items, operations, members, cases, evidence, registered routes, timeouts, selected algorithms, and source digests fail closed; the child subject's downstream effect envelope is not proven closed.","matching":"Launch only the named witness subject and record its outcome; no native order, match, allocation, cancellation, price, or settlement command is supplied.","price_formation":"Child exit codes, event and coverage counts, exact bytes and digests; no price, currency, lot, or quantity unit is assumed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as MARKET because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose market effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without claiming a native market or real trading authority. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.3-settlement-and-disruption":{"declaration":{"disruption":"Stop at the bounded child result, preserve evidence, repair the selected witness, and rerun without retrying market effects.","finality":"Only the witness receipt commits; no order, match, price, allocation, or settlement finality is claimed.","participant_failure":"Unobserved, unauthorized, unavailable, timed-out, or nonzero child behavior is FAIL or UNKNOWN and never becomes evidence of market safety or settlement.","settlement_dependencies":"The selected child subject and any market-like endpoints it can reach; reach is not a grant of authority."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:56d8b831daadf1edfd2d8ed7a678ab129dd36b4f043fac0e74bf92eb85b62c90","reason":"verifier-core-self applies as MARKET because witness_runner.py launches caller-selected subject code whose market effects are not proven unreachable; applicability retains the obligations without claiming a native market or real trading authority. This Tier-0 declaration names the exact reviewed source boundary only; mechanism execution, declaration truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.1-phenomenon-and-method":{"declaration":{"method":"The retained core source set parses exact bounded inputs and derives digital counts, digests, signature results, route outcomes, gaps, and typed status without treating supplied labels as observations.","observation_vs_estimate":"retained VERIFIER digital measurement surface reports only the parent-boundary observations named here. Measurements are bounded digital checker observations from 