cision is distinct from source-role evidence and establishes neither a concrete mechanism, authority, external effect, occurrence, checker PASS, nor Tier-1-plus fulfillment. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.1-phenomenon-and-method":{"declaration":{"method":"bench.evaluate(check=\"budgets\") compares execution_ms and peak_memory_bytes with declared ceilings; oracle/coverage checks recompute outcomes and weighted scores.","observation_vs_estimate":"Resource values are retained claimed observations and scores are checker-derived; neither proves live execution, answer authorship, or population capability.","phenomenon":"Retained per-problem execution duration and peak memory plus recomputed native-oracle outcomes and exact weighted solved fraction.","source":"Caller-selected retained run rows bound to exact problem digests and answers; the checker does not execute or observe the candidate system."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8e737c0f1e2a6f093406aeff53e6dbfc1593fb4896ade68be337a02c756a487","reason":"bench.evaluate(check=\"budgets\") validates retained execution_ms and peak_memory_bytes against declared bounds, while oracle/coverage derives exact weighted scores; live execution and measurement authenticity remain excluded. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"The checker reads the retained rows during evaluation and retains no independent arrival timestamp.","observation_time":"Retained runs include duration but no acquisition timestamp; when or where a candidate ran is not established.","reference_frame":"The exact selected BENCH problem/run inventory, problem digest, native oracle, weight, timeout, memory ceiling, and minimum score.","uncertainty":"Resource claims have no authenticity/error model; rational scoring is exact and only reported-score agreement uses the fixed 1e-12 parsed-value tolerance.","units":"Execution time is milliseconds, peak memory is bytes, oracle work/counts are dimensionless, and score is an exact rational with a dimensionless display."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8e737c0f1e2a6f093406aeff53e6dbfc1593fb4896ade68be337a02c756a487","reason":"bench.evaluate(check=\"budgets\") validates retained execution_ms and peak_memory_bytes against declared bounds, while oracle/coverage derives exact weighted scores; live execution and measurement authenticity remain excluded. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"No freshness window exists; a retained run remains a historical claim and cannot be treated as a current live execution observation.","missingness":"Incomplete suite coverage or unsupported oracle is unavailable; unbound runs, invalid answers, and over-ceiling observations are explicit refutations, not imputations.","provenance":"Tier-0 binds bench.py/bench_checks.py plus exact problem/run/evidence digests; candidate execution, authorship, hardware enforcement, and physical isolation remain excluded.","validity":"Exact problem/run coverage and digest binding, supported oracle, positive weights and ceilings, finite values, resource bounds, and minimum score are required."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8e737c0f1e2a6f093406aeff53e6dbfc1593fb4896ade68be337a02c756a487","reason":"bench.evaluate(check=\"budgets\") validates retained execution_ms and peak_memory_bytes against declared bounds, while oracle/coverage derives exact weighted scores; live execution and measurement authenticity remain excluded. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Selected BENCH/collection records, problem specifications, retained runs/answers, attempt bounds/metrics/selections, resource observations, pins, and limits.","defaults":"Missing coverage, unsupported oracle/metric, duplicate attempt, over-bound resource, incorrect answer, or unavailable evidence cannot default to PASS.","precedence":"Exact problem/run binding precedes oracle, resource, score, or coverage decisions; attempt selection recomputes scores before earliest-retained tie breaking.","scope":"Admission of exact retained BENCH problem/run coverage, native oracle outcomes, resource ceilings, and bounded best-of-N attempt selection."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:76f7bf5ea6d954ce4288935fd317992a7a68eec361dff5211dcc35fefb1efe57","reason":"BENCH evaluate/oracle, bench_attempts best-of-N/metric/tie-break rules, and contract _policy()/request/recheck paths enforce exact current pins, trust roots, finite bounds, and fail-closed retained benchmark decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"Exact current mechanism/source pins, accepted trust roots, supported certificate bound, and selected check activate the finite BENCH policy.","authority":"The caller selects retained benchmark evidence and trust roots; the checker has no candidate-execution, authorship, hardware, ranking, or release authority.","exceptions":"Only named built-in oracles/metrics and exact selected bounds apply; no implicit exception bypasses problem, run, attempt, score, or limit equality.","revisions":"Coordinate and current source/mechanism digests bind the active checker revision; changed source requires a newly selected policy."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:76f7bf5ea6d954ce4288935fd317992a7a68eec361dff5211dcc35fefb1efe57","reason":"BENCH evaluate/oracle, bench_attempts best-of-N/metric/tie-break rules, and contract _policy()/request/recheck paths enforce exact current pins, trust roots, finite bounds, and fail-closed retained benchmark decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unretained attempts, unsupported metrics, stale digests, or reported score alone cannot bypass recomputation and exact selected bounds.","decision_evidence":"Exact problem/run/attempt bytes, recomputed oracle and score results, resource rows, selected policy, and current checker bytes support the local verdict.","enforcement_points":"bench.evaluate(), bench.oracle(), bench_attempts selection, contract _policy()/request parsers, builders, and rechecks enforce the retained benchmark rules.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable or incomplete retained evidence remains UNKNOWN/unavailable and supplies no live execution, authorship, physical isolation, or generalization claim."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:76f7bf5ea6d954ce4288935fd317992a7a68eec361dff5211dcc35fefb1efe57","reason":"BENCH evaluate/oracle, bench_attempts best-of-N/metric/tie-break rules, and contract _policy()/request/recheck paths enforce exact current pins, trust roots, finite bounds, and fail-closed retained benchmark decisions. This declaration records the reviewed Tier-0 boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"The BENCH verifier retains PROTOCOL.participants as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative APPLIES while the owned closed-effect boundary is open. The concrete mechanism value and any external occurrence remain NOT_ESTABLISHED.","roles":"The BENCH verifier retains PROTOCOL.roles as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative APPLIES while the owned cl