pture records launch state, return code, stream lengths and digests, and declared gaps; those are bounded process-interface observations, not whole-subject truth. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"Streams and terminal state arrive when the parent subprocess call returns or raises; no real-time latency guarantee is exported.","observation_time":"Launch and terminal interface phases are ordered, but no trusted wall-clock observation timestamp is claimed.","reference_frame":"One parent launch identity, resolved working-directory digest, declared command, and parent-visible process interface.","uncertainty":"Tri-state and completeness fields retain UNKNOWN, PARTIAL, and UNOBSERVED rather than assigning certainty outside the interface.","units":"Stream lengths and retention limits are bytes; timeout is seconds; return code is an operating-system process-interface integer."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f8af81fe487809679906635d8744567eb86ee7ccce56651da4ae0ccca7af5eec","reason":"Parent-side capture records launch state, return code, stream lengths and digests, and declared gaps; those are bounded process-interface observations, not whole-subject truth. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"Each execution receives a fresh parent-generated launch identity; a prior receipt cannot prove a current launch.","missingness":"Unobserved streams or effects remain explicit null/UNOBSERVED/UNKNOWN values; they are never replaced by empty bytes or NO.","provenance":"The observation binds exact parent-captured values and source bytes but provides integrity, not subject identity authentication or whole-HARNESS truth.","validity":"Exact canonical fields, launch binding, state combinations, stream digest/length, retention semantics, and inner digest must recheck."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f8af81fe487809679906635d8744567eb86ee7ccce56651da4ae0ccca7af5eec","reason":"Parent-side capture records launch state, return code, stream lengths and digests, and declared gaps; those are bounded process-interface observations, not whole-subject truth. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Manifest command/cwd/inputs/outputs/resources, selected language and optional backend, object role, source bindings, and captured outcome.","defaults":"Python is the default language runner, optional backends require explicit selection, and absence of evidence does not establish confinement or external-effect absence.","precedence":"Schema/source/precondition failures refuse before launch; typed launch/runtime failures precede receipt claims; unobserved channels never default to safe.","scope":"Local command admission, language/backend selection, object-role controls, timeout/output bounds, process observation, and receipt/reproduction behavior."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:152f69a6bed895ec692f80ca4ec1fbd6de8c2dd298c6ee9d7eaa9a71158ae05c","reason":"Manifest validation, runner selection, object-role controls, timeouts, and observation requirements are installed decision rules enforced before and after launch. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"Rules activate per invocation and receipt; no persistent approval, deployment, publication, or release authority follows.","authority":"The local operator and host configuration choose the command and runner; this policy grants no authority over subject-owned external resources.","exceptions":"Object-role controls and required bindings cannot be bypassed by relabeling; optional backend absence stays explicit.","revisions":"Installed runner, extension, observation, and validation source define the active revision and are bound by current-source review."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:152f69a6bed895ec692f80ca4ec1fbd6de8c2dd298c6ee9d7eaa9a71158ae05c","reason":"Manifest validation, runner selection, object-role controls, timeouts, and observation requirements are installed decision rules enforced before and after launch. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unknown fields, invalid paths, missing inputs, unavailable runner, stale source, malformed observation, and mismatched outputs cannot silently pass.","decision_evidence":"Receipts retain selected inputs, source and output digests, parent process observation, declared refutation surface, and typed outcome.","enforcement_points":"Manifest validation, runner resolution, prelaunch checks, subprocess capture, output validation, receipt construction, rehash, and rerun selection.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable backend, compiler, interpreter, or evidence remains a typed failure/UNKNOWN boundary and never proves the subject safe."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:152f69a6bed895ec692f80ca4ec1fbd6de8c2dd298c6ee9d7eaa9a71158ae05c","reason":"Manifest validation, runner selection, object-role controls, timeouts, and observation requirements are installed decision rules enforced before and after launch. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Local caller, HARNESS, selected language runner/backend, subject process, and receipt/reproduction consumer.","roles":"Caller selects; HARNESS validates and observes; runner translates the launch; subject executes; receipt consumer rechecks or explicitly reruns.","states":"Draft validation, launch prepared, launch attempted, process start known/unknown, terminal interface outcome, receipt publication, rehash, and explicit rerun.","transitions":"Only validated inputs reach launch; typed outcomes reach receipt construction; rehash reads while rerun deliberately creates a fresh launch."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:fde728c989250ccb3837a890dafc3427308ff1e1b1586d9d764d2692d8bace1f","reason":"Core run, rerun, language-extension, and receipt exchange define local caller, runner, subject, and response states with exact compatibility and failure boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact manifest, receipt, process-observation, runner, and extension schema/version checks replace implicit negotiation.","message_authority":"Local configuration and installed runner selection are trust assumptions; stream bytes and digests do not authenticate the subject actor.","ordering":"One launch observation precedes its receipt; sequential receipt files have no atomic group ordering or distributed consensus claim.","replay":"Rehash never executes; explicit rerun repeats the stored command with a fresh launch identity and can repeat subject effects."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:fde728c989250ccb3837a890dafc3427308ff1e1b1586d9d764d2692d8bace1f","reason":"Core run, rerun, language-extension, and receipt exchange define local caller, runner, subject, and response states with exact compatibility and failure boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The host, selected interpreter/compiler, subprocess API, filesystem, and optional backend remain explicit dependencies.","liveness":"Timeout bounds the parent wait but does not prove descendant termination, backend availability, or whole-subject progress.","recovery":"Failures remain typed and inspectable; only an explicit new invocation retries, and partial receipt publication may require operator repair.","safety":"Malformed input, stale binding, invalid observation, missing output, or incompatible runner cannot silently yield a conforming receipt."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:fde728c989250ccb3837a890dafc3427308ff1e1b1586d9d764d2692d8bace1f","reason":"Core run, rerun, language-extension, and receipt exchange define local caller, runner, subject, and response states with exact compatibility and failure boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:714b130f574101cfac4d448e8397ec396a25bbef3a873de6e68bf893c6b94521","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-harness-99c992c98aee; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:714b130f574101cfac4d448e8397ec396a25bbef3a873de6e68bf893c6b94521","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-harness-99c992c98aee; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.3-consequences-and-intervention":{"declaration":{"hazards":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","intervention":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","safe_state_or_continuity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:714b130f574101cfac4d448e8397ec396a25bbef3a873de6e68bf893c6b94521","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-harness-99c992c98aee; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.1-acquisition-and-observations":{"declaration":{"acquisition":"The parent subprocess interface captures launch outcome, return code, stdout, stderr, timeout fragments, and exception phase around one invocation.","deployment":"Local HARNESS parent and selected runner/backend; no hostile-host isolation, process-tree ownership, or remote sensor claim.","measurements":"Launch/process tri-states, return code, stream availability/completeness, byte counts, digests, and bounded retained prefixes.","phenomena":"Only parent-visible process-interface events and bytes, not descendant behavior or external effects."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f8af81fe487809679906635d8744567eb86ee7ccce56651da4ae0ccca7af5eec","reason":"The parent subprocess interface is the acquisition mechanism for HARNESS process observations and explicitly enumerates descendants, network, undeclared filesystem, and external effects as unobserved. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.2-calibration-and-envelope":{"declaration":{"calibration_applicability":"Physical calibration is inapplicable to this software interface; semantic completeness is bounded by documented observable and unobserved channels.","calibration_evidence":"Controlled completed, nonzero, timeout, launch-error, post-processing-error, truncation, and malformed-record cases test interface-state correspondence.","drift":"Current source digests and schema validation detect implementation drift; operating-system or runtime semantic drift is not certified away.","operating_range":"Positive bounded timeouts, nonnegative retention limits, canonical bounded records, and the selected runner's declared language/runtime surface."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f8af81fe487809679906635d8744567eb86ee7ccce56651da4ae0ccca7af5eec","reason":"The parent subprocess interface is the acquisition mechanism for HARNESS process observations and explicitly enumerates descendants, network, undeclared filesystem, and external effects as unobserved. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.3-sampling-and-faults":{"declaration":{"fault_detection":"Impossible state combinations, digest/length mismatches, missing required fields, and substituted launch bindings refute the record.","latency":"The caller-selected positive timeout bounds the wait; no scheduling or real-time response guarantee is made.","recovery":"A failed capture stays typed as failure or uncertainty; a new invocation gets a new identity and does not repair or authenticate the prior one.","sampling":"One acquisition per parent invocation, with complete terminal streams when available and explicitly partial fragments on timeout."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f8af81fe487809679906635d8744567eb86ee7ccce56651da4ae0ccca7af5eec","reason":"The parent subprocess interface is the acquisition mechanism for HARNESS process observations and explicitly enumerates descendants, network, undeclared filesystem, and external effects as unobserved. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"Explicit local operator invocation and configured backend selection authorize the HARNESS call only; authority over undeclared filesystem, network, descendant, or external subject effects is not established.","effects":"Launch or relaunch the selected subject and sequentially publish its receipt bundle; undeclared subject effects remain explicitly unobserved.","preconditions":"Validate command, working directory, declared inputs, selected runner or backend, timeout, and source bindings before launch; subject-side preconditions are not established.","resources":"Selected child working directory and declared paths, receipt directory, and temporary compiler artifacts; inherited environment and input, descendants, network, undeclared filesystem, and external effects remain unobserved."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f6381681afa525471c110f208d98ac23a23b348d4e0156f565fb378e81b942e9","reason":"The HARNESS launches and can relaunch arbitrary subjects and sequentially publishes receipts, requiring explicit effect, authority, partial-failure, and replay boundaries; process exit is not transaction commit or finality. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Prelaunch validation can refuse launch, and timeout or launch errors bound the parent call; none rolls back, compensates, or proves absence of subject effects already produced.","commit":"A child exit and parent receipt are observations, not transactional commit; receipt files are written sequentially rather than as one atomic publication.","finality":"No subject or global finality is claimed. A completed child remains completed when output hashing or later receipt processing fails.","partial_failure":"A subject can change undeclared resources before nonzero exit, timeout, or post-processing failure, and sequential receipt writes can remain partial; no general compensation mechanism is present."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f6381681afa525471c110f208d98ac23a23b348d4e0156f565fb378e81b942e9","reason":"The HARNESS launches and can relaunch arbitrary subjects and sequentially publishes receipts, requiring explicit effect, authority, partial-failure, and replay boundaries; process exit is not transaction commit or finality. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"There is no cross-invocation duplicate guard; caller-selected or default receipt identifiers and output overwrites do not prevent repeating subject effects.","idempotency":"Idempotency is not assumed. Repeated run, explicit rerun, backend, or language-extension invocation can repeat arbitrary subject effects and overwrite declared artifacts.","replay":"The rerun path deliberately executes the stored command again; the read-only rehash path does not execute, and neither path proves subject idempotency.","retry_limits":"Core capture performs no automatic subject retry and bounds each parent wait by the declared timeout; fresh operator invocations and explicit rerun remain possible."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f6381681afa525471c110f208d98ac23a23b348d4e0156f565fb378e81b942e9","reason":"The HARNESS launches and can relaunch arbitrary subjects and sequentially publishes receipts, requiring explicit effect, authority, partial-failure, and replay boundaries; process exit is not transaction commit or finality. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"direct_launch_denominator":{"launches":[{"call_sha256":"sha256:6cfc63091a06491789ac3c676cbe47b423835df39be943746e5a77083df1ab3c","callee":"subprocess.run","container_sha256":"sha256:31efb5309fd781ce6ab46177b49dae74de3eda0e4211685a6cc6d885ed1fc895","embedded_name":"WORKER","launch_id":"extensions/languages/src/vstd_languages/__init__.py::WORKER|scope=<module>|callee=subprocess.run|ordinal=1","line":30,"necessity_reason":"The language worker must invoke the selected compiler in its fresh artifact directory.","observation_disposition":"SOURCE_ENUMERATION_ONLY","ordinal":1,"path":"extensions/languages/src/vstd_languages/__init__.py","scope":"<module>","source_ast_sha256":"sha256:82a52519ba0e871a034cdcdfd7115163aa4f579c92ecbaec154271f3be6514b6","source_kind":"embedded-python-literal","source_sha256":"sha256:fe4424f4ac01a2a2226130960778d36b0d