HED","finality":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","participant_failure":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","settlement_dependencies":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1e88b099b9ef8332c53780d0565104ab2b721b8fbbb207ff7038250a558b93c","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-simulation-9340543605a7; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MEASUREMENT-0.1-phenomenon-and-method":{"declaration":{"method":"CPython thread_time_ns differences and per-transition tracemalloc peak readings.","observation_vs_estimate":"Direct local instrument readings, not budget counters or extrapolated physical-device usage.","phenomenon":"Resource use within each selected finite interpreter transition, not validation or process startup.","source":"Fresh source-loaded sim_fresh_worker validated by sim_resource_fresh and its closed bootstrap."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM resource path directly samples executing-thread CPU intervals and traced Python allocation peaks for each selected transition, with an explicitly bounded software-only interpretation. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"Parent receives the bounded completed-process response; no absolute arrival timestamp or latency guarantee is exported.","observation_time":"Each transition interval; elapsed thread time is not a wall-clock timestamp.","reference_frame":"The isolated worker's executing thread and Python allocation tracer, indexed by trajectory step.","uncertainty":"Instrument resolution, tracer overhead, host honesty, and calibration are not established; no zero-error physical accuracy claim.","units":"Thread CPU nanoseconds and peak traced Python allocation bytes; no total resident memory or whole-device claim."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM resource path directly samples executing-thread CPU intervals and traced Python allocation peaks for each selected transition, with an explicitly bounded software-only interpretation. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"New challenge and execution per invocation; no historical-record correspondence or wall-age guarantee.","missingness":"Unavailable execution yields UNKNOWN in certificate recheck; malformed captures refute and never fill missing metrics with zero.","provenance":"Closed checked source bytes compile in the worker; the parent rechecks loaded manifest and current sources, not a collector signature.","validity":"Exact method/interpreter, source bindings, step coverage, and state digests; non-Boolean integer metrics in the declared bounds."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM resource path directly samples executing-thread CPU intervals and traced Python allocation peaks for each selected transition, with an explicitly bounded software-only interpretation. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Request, policy, mechanism/source digests, scenario and collection commitments, witness keys where selected, and finite limits.","defaults":"No physical fidelity, confinement, witness independence, sim-to-real safety, or external effect absence is inferred by default.","precedence":"Structural and binding checks precede execution; contradictions are FAIL; unavailable dependencies or unsupported claims remain UNKNOWN.","scope":"Exact finite SIM trajectory, dynamics, channels, shards, response, isolation, and fresh software-resource propositions selected by the caller."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f26c4c6206f92b43e346ad3dbd2bb3431c81b6fbda7b1b12afef63a27b26260a","reason":"Each SIM checker admits only exact request, mechanism, source, trust-root, and finite-limit selections and maps unavailable or contradictory evidence through installed fail-closed rules. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy applies to one selected SIM check and grants no continuing process, physical actuator, or financial authority.","authority":"The local caller selects the proposition and policy; the checker verifies its exact form but does not authenticate external scientific or operational authority.","exceptions":"No exception bypasses source, scenario, signature, finite-bound, or model-replay checks.","revisions":"Policy and installed mechanism/source digests define each active revision; changed bytes require a new selection and run."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f26c4c6206f92b43e346ad3dbd2bb3431c81b6fbda7b1b12afef63a27b26260a","reason":"Each SIM checker admits only exact request, mechanism, source, trust-root, and finite-limit selections and maps unavailable or contradictory evidence through installed fail-closed rules. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unknown fields, missing steps, stale source, invalid signatures, mismatched responses, and exhausted bounds cannot reach PASS.","decision_evidence":"Bounded response and certificate fields retain exact selected commitments, typed outcome, reproduced state/resource observations, and exclusions.","enforcement_points":"Parent request admission, closed source loading, worker execution, response validation, and certificate recheck.","unavailable_behavior":"Unavailable execution, dependency, calibration, or external truth remains UNKNOWN rather than being coerced into a simulated success."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:f26c4c6206f92b43e346ad3dbd2bb3431c81b6fbda7b1b12afef63a27b26260a","reason":"Each SIM checker admits only exact request, mechanism, source, trust-root, and finite-limit selections and maps unavailable or contradictory evidence through installed fail-closed rules. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"The parent verifier, closed bootstrap, fresh SIM worker, selected scenario, and optional named shard witnesses.","roles":"Parent binds inputs and validates output; bootstrap loads closed source; worker executes; shard witnesses sign only their retained coordinates.","states":"Captured request, source validation, worker launch, transition replay, response construction, parent validation, and refusal/unknown terminal states.","transitions":"Only exact schema, source, challenge, request, scenario, step, and response correspondence permits an admitted terminal result."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9239c4c2fd7fba4cde70a91e319efc530e84415a5500b0baf886f4f8517b1294","reason":"The closed bootstrap, fresh worker, bounded response, and optional shard-signature exchange form explicit local participant, ordering, compatibility, failure, and replay boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact installed request, response, certificate, and shard schemas are required; no implicit version negotiation occurs.","message_authority":"Local source selection and configured witness keys are explicit trust assumptions; a digest or shard signature is not independent authority.","ordering":"One bounded request and terminal response frame each run; trajectory and shard rows are indexed in causal-step order.","replay":"Fresh challenges and current-source commitments reject substituted responses; a new run deliberately recomputes the selected scenario."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9239c4c2fd7fba4cde70a91e319efc530e84415a5500b0baf886f4f8517b1294","reason":"The closed bootstrap, fresh worker, bounded response, and optional shard-signature exchange form explicit local participant, ordering, compatibility, failure, and replay boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The host interpreter, filesystem, subprocess transport, and selected witness keys are trusted only within the stated local boundary.","liveness":"Finite process timeouts bound waiting but do not guarantee host scheduling, worker success, or distributed progress.","recovery":"Failure yields FAIL or UNKNOWN as typed; recovery is a newly bound run, never automatic acceptance or hidden retry.","safety":"Malformed, stale, reordered, omitted, substituted, or invalidly signed coordinates cannot supply a validated response."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9239c4c2fd7fba4cde70a91e319efc530e84415a5500b0baf886f4f8517b1294","reason":"The closed bootstrap, fresh worker, bounded response, and optional shard-signature exchange form explicit local participant, ordering, compatibility, failure, and replay boundaries. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1e88b099b9ef8332c53780d0565104ab2b721b8fbbb207ff7038250a558b93c","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-simulation-c89b298ee53a; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1e88b099b9ef8332c53780d0565104ab2b721b8fbbb207ff7038250a558b93c","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-simulation-c89b298ee53a; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.3-consequences-and-intervention":{"declaration":{"hazards":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","intervention":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","safe_state_or_continuity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e1e88b099b9ef8332c53780d0565104ab2b721b8fbbb207ff7038250a558b93c","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-simulation-c89b298ee53a; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.1-acquisition-and-observations":{"declaration":{"acquisition":"Isolated CPython transition execution with per-step thread-clock and allocation-tracer acquisition.","deployment":"Local source-loaded subprocess under the invoking host; not hostile-host isolation or an external physical transducer.","measurements":"Indexed input/output state digests, thread_cpu_ns, and traced_peak_bytes, with run identity.","phenomena":"Executing-thread CPU interval and traced Python allocation peak within that transition."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM worker is the acquisition mechanism for those software-counter observations; it is not a physical sensor and claims no external calibration. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.2-calibration-and-envelope":{"declaration":{"calibration_applicability":"Physical metrology calibration is outside the software-counter interpretation claim; accuracy or external-phenomenon claims need additional evidence.","calibration_evidence":"Controlled instrument inputs check software arithmetic and interval placement, not operating-system clock accuracy or tracer completeness.","drift":"Exact implementation and interpreter bindings detect changed selections; numerical clock drift is neither measured nor certified.","operating_range":"CPython finite replay bounds: at most 100000 operations and 4096 items; accepted nonnegative metrics through 2**63-1."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM worker is the acquisition mechanism for those software-counter observations; it is not a physical sensor and claims no external calibration. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.3-sampling-and-faults":{"declaration":{"fault_detection":"Clock, transition, tracer, process, and binding failures cannot produce a validated complete capture.","latency":"The selected subprocess timeout is 15 seconds; no real-time delivery guarantee is made.","recovery":"Tracing is stopped after started acquisition; another recheck starts a new process. No in-place repair or failover is claimed.","sampling":"One before/after thread-clock pair and allocation peak per transition; replay validation precedes tracing."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh SIM worker is the acquisition mechanism for those software-counter observations; it is not a physical sensor and claims no external calibration. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"The local caller authorizes this fresh resource-verification invocation only; no physical, financial, network, or undeclared filesystem effect authority is established.","effects":"Launch one fresh bounded resource worker and return its local response/certificate bytes; the enclosed pure model transition is subject computation, not itself a transactional effect.","preconditions":"Exact request, policy, resource mechanism, scenario, interpreter, and closed bootstrap/worker source bindings plus finite limits must validate before a response is admitted.","resources":"The fresh local interpreter process, supplied finite scenario, traced Python allocations, thread clock, and parent/worker response channel."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh resource-verification path launches a bounded worker and validates its response, which creates process and response-publication failure boundaries. Pure SIM replay and model-state transition are not themselves classified as transactions. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Validation failure, worker error, malformed response, or timeout refuses the result, but does not prove rollback of unobserved host effects.","commit":"A validated worker response commits no external transaction; it records one completed fresh resource-verification observation around selected model computation.","finality":"Process exit and certificate creation are not physical, financial, distributed, or persistent-state finality.","partial_failure":"A worker may finish computation before response parsing or parent validation fails; the capture is then unadmitted and no external compensation is claimed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh resource-verification path launches a bounded worker and validates its response, which creates process and response-publication failure boundaries. Pure SIM replay and model-state transition are not themselves classified as transactions. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Request, source, challenge, scenario and response commitments distinguish captures; they do not create a global duplicate-execution ledger.","idempotency":"The enclosed selected transition replay is deterministic, but fresh process invocation, observation, and arbitrary host effects are not declared idempotent.","replay":"A recheck starts a fresh process against current bound source; historical signatures or process exit cannot substitute for fresh execution.","retry_limits":"The mechanism performs no hidden automatic retry and bounds each worker invocation by its finite timeout and resource limits."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b5f016b92b7b8b1b17e20c6fb5185ed4423684f25934dad43bc6d637c88461a","reason":"The fresh resource-verification path launches a bounded worker and validates its response, which creates process and response-publication failure boundaries. Pure SIM replay and model-state transition are not themselves classified as transactions. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{"data":["vstd-data"],"env":["vstd-environment"],"objects":["vstd-package-object"],"verifier":["verifier-core-self"]},"payload":{"representation_role":"simulation-representation"},"reason":"Retained package role: simulation-representation. Source ownership enumerates its representation; operational truth remains a higher-tier question.","specializations":["MEASUREMENT","SENSOR","TRANSACTION","ACTUATOR","PROTOCOL","POLICY","FINBOT"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/domains/contracts/sim_checker.py","python:src/verifier/domains/contracts/sim_checker.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/domains/contracts/sim_checker.p