he retained SIM action sequence; no physical endpoint is selected."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT actuation check binds each retained AGENT invocation input to a SIM action. This is a simulated-only command-to-transition boundary and cannot establish a physical effect. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.2-response-and-limits":{"declaration":{"limits":"Only finite retained transitions, records, invocations, actions, observation channels, child certificate bytes and checker operations are admitted.","response":"The next retained SIM projection is compared with the corresponding HARNESS invocation output for the attributed transition.","saturation":"No simulated actuator saturation, rate limit or magnitude clamp is modeled by these BOT sources; absent semantics remain unestablished rather than assumed safe.","units_and_frames":"Transition and HARNESS record indices are dimensionless and action payloads retain the SIM contract's selected frame; no physical unit or coordinate is inferred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT actuation check binds each retained AGENT invocation input to a SIM action. This is a simulated-only command-to-transition boundary and cannot establish a physical effect. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.3-feedback-and-interlocks":{"declaration":{"effect_feedback":"Retained SIM observations and HARNESS invocation outputs provide equality evidence for the simulated loop, not proof of a live effect or whole-SIM truth.","failure_states":"Mismatched action or observation, missing invocation, invalid step mapping, out-of-ceiling channel, unavailable child, or fused environment yields FAIL 