, occurrence, checker PASS, nor Tier-1-plus fulfillment. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.1-feedback-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authority":"External selection and current AGENT, HARNESS, SIM and ENV certificates authorize retained replay only; the BOT checker neither runs an agent nor commands a live environment.","commands":"The AGENT's retained HARNESS invocation inputs are bound exactly to the selected SIM action sequence for attributed transitions.","feedback":"SIM projections are compared with the AGENT's retained HARNESS invocation outputs on channels inside the inherited observation ceiling.","objectives":"Establish the selected simulated closed-loop correspondence: every attributed SIM transition is linked to the retained AGENT/HARNESS interaction, while declared exogenous transitions remain separate. No task-optimality objective is inferred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT object is the selected closed loop that binds simulated feedback to AGENT commands across attributed transitions, so its objectives, envelope, timing, stability exclusions and failure behavior require declaration. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.2-timing-and-stability":{"declaration":{"operating_envelope":"The envelope is the exact selected SIM, attributed transition set, inherited AGENT observation ceiling, retained HARNESS records and invocations, current child policies, and declared distinct environments.","saturation":"No command magnitude or actuator saturation model is present. A missing invocation, out-of-ceiling channel, absent attribution, or unsupported child remains FAIL or UNKNOWN rather than clipped control.","stability_assumptions":"No convergence, robustness, bounded-state, reward, controllability, observability, or closed-loop stability theorem is checked; correspondence alone cannot supply one.","timing":"Control order is the strict dimensionless SIM transition and HARNESS record order. No wall-clock rate, deadline, latency, simultaneity, or real-time schedule is established."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT object is the selected closed loop that binds simulated feedback to AGENT commands across attributed transitions, so its objectives, envelope, timing, stability exclusions and failure behavior require declaration. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.3-intervention-and-failure":{"declaration":{"arbitration":"The selected step map and explicit exogenous-transition list divide responsibility between the AGENT and simulation inputs; no multi-controller priority or conflict resolver is claimed.","failure_behavior":"Contradictory bindings FAIL and missing evidence or unestablished separation remains UNKNOWN; no live safe state, continuity guarantee, or corrective action follows from a certificate.","feedback_loss":"A missing or mismatched retained observation, uninstrumented channel, unavailable child, fused environment, or incomplete step map prevents establishment of the loop.","intervention":"The checker can refuse a retained BOT claim. It has no live pause, override, shutdown, human intervention, or command-replacement channel."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT object is the selected closed loop that binds simulated feedback to AGENT commands across attributed transitions, so its objectives, envelope, timing, stability exclusions and failure behavior require declaration. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillme