d establishes neither a concrete mechanism, authority, external effect, occurrence, checker PASS, nor Tier-1-plus fulfillment. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Exact AGENT, SIM, ENV and retained HARNESS certificates; current child policies; observation ceiling, records, invocations, transition attribution, simulated observations and actions, separation declaration, and finite limits.","defaults":"No live execution, physical isolation, stability, task success, corrigibility, real-world actuation, sim-to-real crossing, or historical child-policy reproduction is assumed.","precedence":"Every child and environment binds before alignment; exact mismatches FAIL, while absent attributed transitions, fused environments, or unobserved channels remain UNKNOWN.","scope":"Admission of one retained BOT closed-loop binding among an AGENT, its HARNESS evidence, one SIM, and distinct declared AGENT and SIM environments."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources enforce child identity, transition attribution, observation ceiling, action/observation equality, environment separation and bounded current-policy replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy applies to one bounded retained BOT replay and does not start the AGENT, advance a live SIM, or authorize any external action.","authority":"External selection and current child policies authorize only this retained replay. The BOT record grants no physical, financial, deployment, or live-agent authority.","exceptions":"No exception invents an unattributed step, widens the AGENT ceiling, merges distinct environments, or substitutes a SIM observation or action.","revisions":"Current mechanism, source, policy and child-certificate digests bind the loop; a changed AGENT, SIM, HARNESS or ENV selection is a different BOT."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources enforce child identity, transition attribution, observation ceiling, action/observation equality, environment separation and bounded current-policy replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Missing invocations, unbound transitions, out-of-ceiling channels, substituted children, fused environments, and exhausted limits cannot silently pass.","decision_evidence":"The certificate binds every selected child and reports only attributed and exogenous transitions, observation ceiling, declared environment separation, and bounded outcome.","enforcement_points":"Request and policy parsing, child replay, HARNESS digest binding, transition attribution, strict record order, observation and action equality, environment separation, inherited ceiling, and exact recheck.","unavailable_behavior":"A loop with no attributed transition, unavailable child, fused environment, or unobserved channel remains UNKNOWN rather than being treated as contained or controlled."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources enforce child identity, transition attribution, observation ceiling, action/observation equality, environment separation and bounded current-policy replay. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Externally selected AGENT, its retained HARNESS interaction, selected SIM, AGENT ENV, SIM ENV, BOT checker and certificate rechecker.","roles":"The AGENT supplies retained decisions and invocations, HARNESS supplies witnessed records, SIM supplies transitions/actions/projections, ENV records support separation, and BOT binds their correspondence.","states":"Children-bound, transitions-partitioned, step-map-aligned, initial-observation-bound, action-and-observation-compared, environment-separation-checked, and certificate accepted, failed or unavailable.","transitions":"Exact child replay permits alignment; strict retained record order permits each attributed transition comparison; optional containment advances only when declared distinct environments remain separately evidenced."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources define participant roles, strict transition/record ordering, replay compatibility and failure handling across AGENT, HARNESS, SIM and ENV certificates. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact AGENT, SIM, HARNESS and ENV kinds, subject ids, digests, current route versions, action and observation shapes, channel names, and finite bounds must agree.","message_authority":"Current child certificates, object and evidence digests, external policy and trust-root selections authorize interpretation of retained interaction bytes only.","ordering":"SIM transitions preserve their sequence, attributed HARNESS record indices must strictly increase, the initial observation precedes attributed steps, and child binding precedes every comparison.","replay":"Build and recheck replay exact retained child certificates and interaction evidence under current policies; historical child-policy reproduction is explicitly not established."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources define participant roles, strict transition/record ordering, replay compatibility and failure handling across AGENT, HARNESS, SIM and ENV certificates. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"Only retained child and parent-interface evidence is observed; live scheduling, hidden environment channels, physical isolation, sim-to-real effects and external side effects remain outside the protocol claim.","liveness":"Finite replay terminates under checker bounds, but no claim says an AGENT acts, a SIM advances, the loop remains available, or a task eventually succeeds.","recovery":"Unavailable or contradictory exchanges require corrected selections or evidence and a complete fresh replay; there is no live reconnect, retry, compensation, or system reset.","safety":"No unattributed transition is silently assigned to the AGENT, no uninstrumented channel supports the loop, and action or observation disagreement cannot pass."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:abbbdffceb443bfcb2ef93699caf6953b68ff28e4f9fa73c29a0534449245b39","reason":"The BOT sources define participant roles, strict transition/record ordering, replay compatibility and failure handling across AGENT, HARNESS, SIM and ENV certificates. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"The vstd-bot verifier retains ROBOT.actuators as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative APPLIES while the owned closed-effect boundary is open. The concrete mechanism value and any external occurrence remain NOT_ESTABLISHED.","agent":"The vstd-bot verifier retains ROBOT.agent as a Tier-0 obligation because the sole authored reasons.vstd selects conservative 