ecedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Exact token records, issuing keys admitted by checker policy, accepted algorithms, birth commitment, epoch and status traces, root scopes, audiences, clock and skew, caveats, windows, replay identifiers, and finite limits.","defaults":"A signature binds bytes to an admitted key but is never an authority grant; possession, scope text, status, or a TOKEN label grants no legal, financial, physical, or application authority by default.","precedence":"Inventory shape and unique identifiers bind first; signature and delegation contradictions FAIL, while missing keys, unsupported algorithms, stale statuses, clock ambiguity, or incomplete tenure remain UNKNOWN.","scope":"Admission of one retained capability-token holding: identity, tenure fold, delegation attenuation, signatures, audiences, time windows, caveats, status freshness, and replay relations."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"The TOKEN sources apply externally selected keys, algorithms, trust roots, scope attenuation, caveats, windows, replay ids, clock skew, status freshness and finite limits without turning a signature into authority. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The policy evaluates one retained holding and grants no invocation, redemption, transfer, spending, settlement, or application access by itself.","authority":"The external checker policy admits exact public keys, algorithms and witness mappings; the token bundle cannot admit its own issuer or prove the issuer's real authority.","exceptions":"No exception permits unsigned algorithms, key confusion, scope widening, dropped caveats, re-delegated soulbound leases, stale status, replay-id collision, or out-of-window use.","revisions":"Current source, mechanism, policy, admitted key set, accepted algorithms and selected clock/status inputs bind the rules; changed policy or observations require fresh review."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"The TOKEN sources apply externally selected keys, algorithms, trust roots, scope attenuation, caveats, windows, replay ids, clock skew, status freshness and finite limits without turning a signature into authority. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Unspecified issuers, unsupported algorithms, absent or stale statuses, delegation gaps, clock ambiguity, malformed signatures, and exhausted limits cannot silently become authorized.","decision_evidence":"Certificates bind exact retained token and status bytes, admitted policy and mechanism digests, and the bounded tenure, lease, signature, closure, or projection result.","enforcement_points":"Canonical inventory parsing, unique token and replay ids, epoch folding, delegation graph and attenuation, key and signature checks, audience and window closure, status freshness, native projection, and exact recheck.","unavailable_behavior":"Missing authority evidence, unsupported verification, incomplete epochs, stale status, uncertain window phase, or absent lease closure remains UNKNOWN rather than being treated as valid or revoked."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"The TOKEN sources apply externally selected keys, algorithms, trust roots, scope attenuation, caveats, windows, replay ids, clock skew, status freshness and finite limits without turning a signature into authority. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"Recorded issuer keys, birth issuer, delegating and delegate keys, token holders, named audiences, status publishers, external policy selector, TOKEN checker and certificate rechecker.","roles":"Issuers sign canonical records, parents attenuate leases, delegates receive constrained claims, status publishers report state, policy admits keys/algorithms, and the checker replays the bounded relations.","states":"Birth, aging and lifetime token forms; pending, open, ended or clock-undetermined windows; ACTIVE, SUSPENDED or REVOKED epoch/status states; and verified, unavailable or refuted replay outcomes.","transitions":"Issuance follows birth, delegation follows an existing parent grant with attenuation, epoch folding advances contiguously, revocation cannot resume, key retirement bounds later issuance, and fresh status updates supersede older ones."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"TOKEN birth, aging, lease delegation, signature, audience, window and status records define participant roles, ordered state transitions, replay resistance, compatibility and fail-closed progress boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact schema and semantic versions, token kinds and fields, supported signature algorithms, key encoding, clock declaration, policy/mechanism digests, native projection mapping and finite bounds must match.","message_authority":"Canonical signatures under policy-admitted exact public keys authorize only attribution of token bytes to that key; they do not prove application or financial authority.","ordering":"Issued-at and parent ordering, contiguous epochs, delegation depth, time windows, key retirement, status publication and freshness are compared on the declared clock with explicit skew.","replay":"Replay identifiers must be unique in the holding, exact retained bytes rebuild each result, and recheck cannot silently substitute a token, key, status, clock, policy or native projection."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"TOKEN birth, aging, lease delegation, signature, audience, window and status records define participant roles, ordered state transitions, replay resistance, compatibility and fail-closed progress boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The protocol sees retained records and policy-admitted keys only; issuer identity, secret-key custody, application enforcement, network delivery, global revocation service and wall-clock truth remain outside evidence.","liveness":"No issuance, delivery, status publication, application acceptance, or eventual recovery is guaranteed; missing or stale necessary evidence remains UNKNOWN.","recovery":"A corrected current holding, key policy, epoch trace or status set must be selected and replayed afresh; the checker performs no revocation broadcast, key rotation, reissue, or application rollback.","safety":"Delegation cannot widen scope/window/invocation bounds, drop or rewrite inherited caveats, re-delegate a soulbound lease, use a retired key, collide replay ids, or hide stale/missing status behind PASS."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:90270fd3b96afed5564e1b079836e90a88d60a955501e614720ed35f73445538","reason":"TOKEN birth, aging, lease delegation, signature, audience, window and status records define participant roles, ordered state transitions, replay resistance, compatibility and fail-closed progress boundaries. This exact-source Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration"