l-byte digests are compared.","sources_and_sinks":"Explicit provisioning creates the ledger; commit_issuance inserts once; policy epochs strictly advance. No deletion API is declared.","units":"Integer invocation counts, retained-byte counts, sequences and policy epochs; no monetary units are represented."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:1ef3036ee28f69068bd4528a7a11241521229a42d543cc1767590c3d090e9423","reason":"The owned source implements the local LEDGER boundary described by the named declarations. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"Advance the policy epoch to invalidate old selections; in-place correction of issuance records is not an offered operation.","reconciliation":"Compare exact proposal, receipt, configured identity, epoch and mechanism digests with retained bytes.","recovery":"Storage unavailability or uncertain commit returns UNKNOWN. Backup restoration and global uniqueness are not established.","replay":"recheck_issuance_commit reads the same row; repeated consumption is refused."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:1ef3036ee28f69068bd4528a7a11241521229a42d543cc1767590c3d090e9423","reason":"The owned source implements the local LEDGER boundary described by the named declarations. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.1-orders-and-access":{"declaration":{"cancellation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","order_states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","participant_access":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","validation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-invocation-ledger-31565fce52f0; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MARKET-0.2-matching-and-allocation":{"declaration":{"allocation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","manipulation_controls":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","matching":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","price_formation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-invocation-ledger-31565fce52f0; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MARKET-0.3-settlement-and-disruption":{"declaration":{"disruption":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","finality":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","participant_failure":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","settlement_dependencies":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-invocation-ledger-31565fce52f0; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MEASUREMENT-0.1-phenomenon-and-method":{"declaration":{"method":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observation_vs_estimate":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","phenomenon":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","source":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-measurement-vstd-invocation-ledger-3c33af5ac154; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observation_time":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","reference_frame":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","uncertainty":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","units":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-measurement-vstd-invocation-ledger-3c33af5ac154; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","missingness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","provenance":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","validity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-measurement-vstd-invocation-ledger-3c33af5ac154; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"IssuerLedgerSelection, exact proposal and status digests, invocation id, commit time, current database state, and fixed capacity ceilings.","defaults":"Candidates cannot choose the ledger path or epoch, and no public authority, worldwide uniqueness, or monetary meaning is assumed.","precedence":"Selection/proposal validation precedes BEGIN IMMEDIATE; known replay is FAIL; capacity or uncertain storage/commit is UNKNOWN.","scope":"One host-provisioned local invocation-consumption ledger, its identity/domain/epoch, and bounded issuance rows."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:1ef3036ee28f69068bd4528a7a11241521229a42d543cc1767590c3d090e9423","reason":"Host-selected ledger identity, policy domain and epoch plus fixed capacity and replay rules govern which local issuance can commit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"The exact selected ledger metadata is checked inside each writable or read-only database operation.","authority":"An authenticated host provisions the absolute non-UNC path, ledger identity, policy domain, and current epoch outside candidate input.","exceptions":"No override bypasses proposal digest, epoch, identity, uniqueness, retained-capacity, or mechanism checks.","revisions":"advance_policy_epoch must strictly increase the stored epoch and invalidates old selections without rewriting issuance history."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:1ef3036ee28f69068bd4528a7a11241521229a42d543cc1767590c3d090e9423","reason":"Host-selected ledger identity, policy domain and epoch plus fixed capacity and replay rules govern which local issuance can commit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Candidate-selected paths, stale epochs, malformed proposals, known replay, mismatched receipts, and changed mechanisms cannot yield PASS.","decision_evidence":"A bounded local receipt binds ledger/domain/epoch, invocation, sequence, proposal/status/time/mechanism digests, and exact retained proposal.","enforcement_points":"Selection validation, SQLite metadata check, transactional uniqueness/capacity check, precommit receipt construction, COMMIT, and read-only recheck.","unavailable_behavior":"Cancellation, storage failure, exhausted bounds, and uncertain commit remain UNKNOWN and require recheck rather than inferred non-consumption."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:1ef3036ee28f69068bd4528a7a11241521229a42d543cc1767590c3d090e9423","reason":"Host-selected ledger identity, policy domain and epoch plus fixed capacity and replay rules govern which local issuance can commit. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"One installed Verifier parent and the fixed local_ledger_worker child selected by verifier-local-invocation-ledger-1; neither participant is an authenticated external authority.","roles":"The parent binds a nonce plus exact object and collection digests, submits the canonical request, captures the process boundary, and checks the response; the child validates the closed request, runs fresh temporary-ledger experiments, and emits observations only.","states":"The ledger-specific exchange advances from a selected source-bound adapter to one validated request, one fresh worker experiment, and either one bound observation response or a rejected, unavailable, nonzero, timed-out, malformed, oversized, or source-changed outcome.","transitions":"Only the installed adapter can select the fixed worker and exact request/response schema versions; caller-supplied commands, database paths, money, subjects, and authority channels are not protocol inputs."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:63eb13fb3a9c28baf21164258f549d2f9b08f768efb59606b26782f224565a3f","reason":"The source-bound execution adapter and fixed worker exchange one versioned bounded JSON request and response across a parent/child process boundary; that protocol needs exact participants, ordering, replay, compatibility and failure limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact verifier-local-ledger-execution-request-1 and verifier-local-ledger-execution-observations-1 versions, closed field sets, echoed request equality, and unchanged source pins are required; no negotiation or permissive fallback is implemented.","message_authority":"Current source pins, the selected mechanism, a fresh nonce, and exact object and collection digests bind the exchange; JSON, SHA-256 digests, and the nonce authenticate no actor, host, or external authority.","ordering":"The parent submits one bounded canonical JSON request on standard input; the worker captures source pins before and after its fresh experiments and emits one bounded JSON observation response on standard output for parent-side binding checks.","replay":"A fresh nonce and current object, collection, selection, and source bindings distinguish each execution. A retained response is evidence of only its captured exchange and is never accepted as fresh execution; the protocol performs no automatic retry."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:63eb13fb3a9c28baf21164258f549d2f9b08f768efb59606b26782f224565a3f","reason":"The source-bound execution adapter and fixed worker exchange one versioned bounded JSON request and response across a parent/child process boundary; that protocol needs exact participants, ordering, replay, compatibility and failure limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The interpreter and host are trusted dependencies. Missing or changed source, launch failure, nonzero exit, timeout, malformed or oversized output, incomplete capture, and request or source-pin mismatch cannot produce accepted observations.","liveness":"No completion or availability guarantee is claimed. The parent timeout only bounds how long one attempt waits; there is no automatic retry, delivery guarantee, worker progress proof, or service-uptime claim.","recovery":"A failed or unavailable exchange remains failed or UNKNOWN for that attempt and requires a separately authorized fresh invocation. Temporary worker resources are scoped to that run; no durable protocol checkpoint or response replay is treated as recovery.","safety":"The fixed worker accepts no caller command, operator database path, money, subject, or authority channel and can issue no package PASS. This is a source-bound process interface, not a sandbox, delivery proof, child-internal observation, or external-effect confinement claim."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:63eb13fb3a9c28baf21164258f549d2f9b08f768efb59606b26782f224565a3f","reason":"The source-bound execution adapter and fixed worker exchange one versioned bounded JSON request and response across a parent/child process boundary; that protocol needs exact participants, ordering, replay, compatibility and failure limits. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:dac8a4f2c7cd1cc40174c73520787bb1f9dab691aaa2d2e95524487a50eaf810","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-invocation-ledger-f4002302b363; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","do