:644f166d1d278264f7b317d1a1cc7eb36e27304eeff3696fb743ab646091e6a4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-policy-vstd-manifest-write-94cc5e290258; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","authority":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","exceptions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","revisions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:644f166d1d278264f7b317d1a1cc7eb36e27304eeff3696fb743ab646091e6a4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-policy-vstd-manifest-write-94cc5e290258; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","decision_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","enforcement_points":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","unavailable_behavior":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:644f166d1d278264f7b317d1a1cc7eb36e27304eeff3696fb743ab646091e6a4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-policy-vstd-manifest-write-94cc5e290258; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"One installed Verifier parent and the fixed manifest_write_worker child selected by verifier-manifest-publication-1; neither endpoint is an authenticated external authority.","roles":"The owned adapter selects the closed request and response versions and delegates transport to the package worker exchange; the fixed child validates the request, runs private-file publication experiments, and emits observations only.","states":"The manifest-specific exchange advances from a source-bound selected adapter to one validated request, one fresh private worker experiment, and either one bound observation response or a rejected, unavailable, nonzero, timed-out, malformed, oversized, or source-changed outcome.","transitions":"Only the installed adapter can select the fixed worker and manifest request/response schemas; caller commands, operator manifests, subject imports, and publication authority are not protocol inputs."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:925e9afa3dac5e78435d6678efac64d4793ffc168985f9e09f4ef15f2ac63895","reason":"The owned manifest adapter and fixed worker are local endpoints of a versioned bounded request/reply exchange delegated to the uniquely owned package worker protocol; participant, ordering, replay, compatibility, failure, and progress boundaries therefore apply without transferring dispatcher ownership. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Exact verifier-manifest-publication-request-1 and verifier-manifest-publication-observations-1 versions, closed field sets, echoed request equality, and unchanged source pins are required; no negotiation or permissive fallback is implemented.","message_authority":"Current source pins, the selected mechanism, a fresh nonce, and exact object and collection digests bind the exchange; JSON and SHA-256 identify bytes but authenticate no actor, host, or external authority.","ordering":"The package worker exchange submits one bounded canonical request before the child runs private-file experiments; the child captures source pins before and after execution and returns one bounded response for parent-side request and source binding checks.","replay":"A fresh nonce plus current object, collection, selection, and source bindings distinguish each execution. Retained observations describe only their captured exchange and are never accepted as a fresh run; no automatic retry is performed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:925e9afa3dac5e78435d6678efac64d4793ffc168985f9e09f4ef15f2ac63895","reason":"The owned manifest adapter and fixed worker are local endpoints of a versioned bounded request/reply exchange delegated to the uniquely owned package worker protocol; participant, ordering, replay, compatibility, failure, and progress boundaries therefore apply without transferring dispatcher ownership. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"The interpreter, host, and delegated package worker transport are trusted dependencies. Missing or changed source, launch failure, nonzero exit, timeout, malformed or oversized output, incomplete capture, and request or source-pin mismatch cannot produce accepted observations.","liveness":"No completion or availability guarantee is claimed. The parent timeout bounds one attempt only; there is no automatic retry, delivery guarantee, child-progress proof, or service-uptime claim.","recovery":"A failed or unavailable exchange remains failed or UNKNOWN for that attempt and requires a separately authorized fresh invocation. Private worker resources are scoped to that run; no retained response is treated as a recovery checkpoint.","safety":"The fixed child accepts no caller command, operator manifest, or subject module and can issue no package PASS. This is a source-bound process interface, not a sandbox, application-authority proof, power-loss durability claim, or external-effect confinement claim."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:925e9afa3dac5e78435d6678efac64d4793ffc168985f9e09f4ef15f2ac63895","reason":"The owned manifest adapter and fixed worker are local endpoints of a versioned bounded request/reply exchange delegated to the uniquely owned package worker protocol; participant, ordering, replay, compatibility, failure, and progress boundaries therefore apply without transferring dispatcher ownership. This Tier-0 declaration names the boundary only; mechanism execution and higher-tier semantic fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:644f166d1d278264f7b317d1a1cc7eb36e27304eeff3696fb743ab646091e6a4","reason":"reasons.