179e14c2d60222230c0 binds exact source src/verifier/hardware/registry.py; source role, necessity, consequence boundary, operands, and path set are hash-bound; declaration text alone establishes no execution truth. Field declaration: vstd-accelerator-profile-registry (Mutable accelerator profile catalog with unsealed Python construction and lookup dispatch.) is limited to in-process values and any files, processes, or endpoints explicitly selected by its owned sources."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2c4dde98a40dc3292db8c031f1cddfcf24ca273efbcd317065cdd9afe526fa11","reason":"vstd-accelerator-profile-registry applies as ACTUATOR because its exact owned source accepts caller-supplied profile objects and performs overridable self.register and cls(...) dispatch; that unsealed runtime boundary is not established to exclude ACTUATOR behavior. This retains the obligation without asserting occurrence, authority, physical or financial effect, publication, or release. Audited semantic basis: vstd-accelerator-profile-registry owns Mutable accelerator profile catalog with unsealed Python construction and lookup dispatch. Exact current source-byte denominator: src/verifier/hardware/registry.py. Fixed operands: none. Necessity: Construction accepts caller-supplied profile objects, invokes overridable self.register, and classmethods dispatch through cls; all delegated consequence roles remain explicit while catalog validation and lookup policy stay bounded. Consequence boundary: Applicability retains obligations without asserting any delegated effect occurred; catalog presence or PASS-shaped data establishes no device fact, caller identity, custody, physical actuation, financial effect, publication, release, or external authority. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed exact-source boundary only; mechanism execution, semantic truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.2-response-and-limits":{"declaration":{"limits":"vstd-accelerator-profile-registry 