 commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: Applicability retains every delegated obligation without claiming a hook or endpoint ran; a projection does not reevaluate evidence, prove provenance, establish identity or authority, or grant conformance. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Repeated reading produces a new projection of current selected bytes; no cached success or duplicate identity is retained.","idempotency":"The accessibility artifact reader treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Correct or replace the selected artifact and rerun; execute the separately named checker when fresh evaluation is required.","retry_limits":"Repeated reading produces a new projection of current selected bytes; no cached success or duplicate identity is retained."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:a65e7009f17029ef2eea94b32233b14d54f0f17b8099497fa815275caca8e7e8","reason":"The accessibility artifact reader applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: Applicability retains every delegated obligation without claiming a hook or endpoint ran; a projection does not reevaluate evidence, prove provenance, establish identity or authority, or grant conformance. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Selected accessibility-artifact acquisition and diagnostic explanation projection."},"reason":"The public handler reads attributes from a caller-supplied namespace and coerces its path without a runtime type seal, so ev