T-0.3-decisions-effects-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"decision_effect_evidence":"Current mechanism and proposition digests, exact policy/request/evidence bindings, selected route and source coordinate, finite retained lifecycle or consequence relationships, worker return status, response bytes, nonce, schema, and source pins where launched, typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN reason, explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED fields, and reproduced certificate digest.","intervention":"Call installed route selection, strict decoding, digest, finite domain-evaluation, consequence-graph assessment, certificate construction, and certificate recheck functions, or launch only the exact installed POLICY observation worker as python -I -S -B; no subject-authored command is executed.","limit_enforcement":"Exact policy, request, proposition, source, mechanism, and evidence digests are checked before strict canonical-JSON decoding; the selected finite domain evaluator and installed consequence-graph engine produce a typed result, and recheck rebuilds the complete self-digested certificate byte for byte. POLICY observation acquisition launches the installed worker as python -I -S -B, sends one nonce-bound request, and verifies its return status, schema, nonce, and source pins.","reconciliation_and_recovery":"Select the exact current route and policy, restore current source/proposition bindings and worker availability, supply a complete bounded canonical retained payload, and perform a fresh full acquisition, build, or recheck; never edit or trust a partial response or certificate. Real-world financial reconciliation and recovery remain NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e073587b46d44f9dd79dd9bf9af9bddc0725bcaaad76466856722e70dfb2e081","reason":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER applies as FINBOT. Its applicable ASSET boundary is reached by the same source-bound certificate route, so effect-first classification retains FINBOT obligations while actual agency, authority, endpoints, exposure, financial effects, and reconciliation remain NOT_ESTABLISHED. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.1-authoritative-history":{"declaration":{"authority":"Installed route and policy code select the proposition, checker, limits, and nonpromotion boundary and authorize only the named local worker launch. Caller-supplied trust-root labels and retained records grant no venue, physical, legal, publication, or release authority; actual financial authority is NOT_ESTABLISHED.","history":"Current mechanism and proposition digests, exact policy/request/evidence bindings, selected route and source coordinate, finite retained lifecycle or consequence relationships, worker return status, response bytes, nonce, schema, and source pins where launched, typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN reason, explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED fields, and reproduced certificate digest.","ordering":"Validate the current policy, mechanism, route, proposition, request, limits, and evidence reference before decoding retained bytes; for observation acquisition, construct the fixed nonce request before the isolated worker launch and accept output only after return-code, schema, nonce, and source-pin checks; evaluate only the selected route; bind the result and nonpromotion fields before the envelope digest; on recheck, validate the envelope and rebuild it exactly before returning.","state":"Unselected, policy-admitted, request-admitted, evidence-unavailable, decoded, evaluated PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN, certificate-built, replay-reproduced, stale, substituted, malformed, limit-exhausted, worker-unavailable, worker-timed-out, worker-failed, and worker-response-refused states remain distinct."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:007780e146ef72134bcddc919e0b9d80736c5150920516d35e38feb0cb3dba7d","reason":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER applies as LEDGER. Its locally authoritative ordered history and recovery behavior would be hidden by a generic object label. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.2-accounting-invariants":{"declaration":{"balance_rules":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER is an ordered event/accounting ledger, not a fungible balance sheet. Its invariant is the exact authorized and ordered commit contract: Commit is only a self-digested canonical certificate for the exact selected request, policy, mechanism, proposition, evidence payload, and bounded result. Every certificate retains object-profile and external-effect claims as NOT_ESTABLISHED.","rounding":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER records exact discrete events and byte digests; it defines no numeric rounding convention or financial balance.","sources_and_sinks":"Launch at most one selected local POLICY observation subprocess per acquisition, write its bounded nonce request to standard input, capture its return code and output, read current checker sources and caller-supplied bytes, compute digests, replay finite retained relationships, and return certificate bytes or a typed refusal without commanding the represented external system.","units":"Evidence and certificate bytes, retained record and trust-root counts, integer price/quantity/exposure/sequence units declared by the retained evidence, and SHA-256 identities; worker timeouts use integer seconds and process completion uses one integer return code."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:007780e146ef72134bcddc919e0b9d80736c5150920516d35e38feb0cb3dba7d","reason":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER applies as LEDGER. Its locally authoritative ordered history and recovery behavior would be hidden by a generic object label. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER does not