-B, sends one nonce-bound request, and verifies its return status, schema, nonce, and source pins.","observation_vs_estimate":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER reports only the parent-boundary observations named here. This is a first-party VERIFIER with bounded local software actuation for one exact isolated POLICY observation worker. Its retained records and certificate lifecycle carry the twelve review-kind roles so their obligations cannot be discarded. These are bounded checker and evidence roles, not promotion to represented subjects: an actual financial or physical AGENT, HARNESS binding, live market participant, venue, financial authority, exposure, real-world endpoint, physical reach, effect, safety, settlement, and reconciliation are NOT_ESTABLISHED. The checker commands no represented subject, performs no external participant exchange, physical actuation, settlement, or real-money movement, and does not establish runtime correspondence; asset backing and custody are NOT_ESTABLISHED. It does not establish full-application polish, publication, release, or deployment.","phenomenon":"Current mechanism and proposition digests, exact policy/request/evidence bindings, selected route and source coordinate, finite retained lifecycle or consequence relationships, worker return status, response bytes, nonce, schema, and source pins where launched, typed PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN reason, explicit NOT_ESTABLISHED fields, and reproduced certificate digest.","source":"An exact kind/check/subject/source selection, current proposition and mechanism digests, an immutable evidence-byte reference, sorted unique trust-root labels, a policy digest, retained asset and party identifiers where selected, and finite evidence-byte, record, and certificate ceilings."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:b036d1856154c8e45c8b749431538700d1c2414556232697b9120ed744ba8728","reason":"added-kind retained-evidence VERIFIER applies as MEASUREMENT. Its retained parent-boundary values distinguish what wa