ation":"Authority is limited to the local caller's path access and explicitly supplied signing key; a valid seal establishes neither ownership nor authorization.","effects":"A successful operation creates a frozen bundle, an exclusive seal record, or a separate mutable descendant; it does not alter the frozen parent's content.","preconditions":"Exact source bytes, normalized relative paths, freeze/seal records, local filesystem metadata, and explicitly supplied key bytes are preconditions.","resources":"Targets are the exact selected source, frozen bundle, seal directory, thaw destination, and sidecar records on the local filesystem."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d2bbbc0aa56de7608031efbce1bc9bef24b59c05b233ea1ae646f7cebf2e7077","reason":"The artifact freeze/seal/thaw lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named local change, response-dependent finality, retry behavior, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Malformed records, path escape, special files, source drift, digest or signature mismatch, guard failure, collision, or write error refuses the selected transition.","commit":"Freeze commits when the complete staging directory is renamed to an absent destination; seal and thaw sidecar records use exclusive creation, but the operations are not one application-wide transaction.","finality":"Freeze commits when the complete staging directory is renamed to an absent destination; seal and thaw sidecar records use exclusive creation, but the operations are not one application-wide transaction. Finality is limited to the named local state and grants no application-wide correctness, publication, physical, or financial authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed records, path escape, special files, source drift, digest or signature mismatch, guard failure, collision, or write error refuses the selected transition."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d2bbbc0aa56de7608031efbce1bc9bef24b59c05b233ea1ae646f7cebf2e7077","reason":"The artifact freeze/seal/thaw lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named local change, response-dependent finality, retry behavior, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Existing destinations and conflicting seal identities refuse rather than overwrite; a retry is a fresh verification and explicitly selected new operation.","idempotency":"Existing destinations and conflicting seal identities refuse rather than overwrite; a retry is a fresh verification and explicitly selected new operation. These are the exact retry semantics; no broader idempotency is inferred.","replay":"Recovery requires correcting the local source, key, record, guard, or destination and starting a new operation; accepted history is not silently rewritten.","retry_limits":"Paths, ordinary-file rules, canonical records, digest equality, read-only guards, key form, and absent destinations bound accepted operations."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d2bbbc0aa56de7608031efbce1bc9bef24b59c05b233ea1ae646f7cebf2e7077","reason":"The artifact freeze/seal/thaw lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named local change, response-dependent finality, retry behavior, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Local artifact freeze, seal and thaw lifecycle plus its duplicated wire schema."},"reason":"Lifecycle state changes have precondition, authority, ordering, duplicate and partial-failure questions that generic artif