c792","reason":"The bounded artifact snapshot mechanism applies as SENSOR. Its bounded software acquisition path has explicit source, range, latency, missingness, and fault behavior. Reviewed boundary: Local exact-byte capture and per-file writing lack provenance authority, locking, crash durability, multi-file atomicity, and any external consequence claim. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"The caller selects readable source and writable destination paths; the code provides no provenance, ownership, publication, locking, or external authority.","effects":"Read a finite local artifact and optionally create or replace individual destination files, or exclusively create one canonical output record.","preconditions":"One caller-selected artifact path, finite ordinary source entries, optional destination path, and an optional canonical JSON record.","resources":"The selected local source tree, in-memory Snapshot, and caller-selected local destination only."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8a3103e9bc3946e155f42077ba5f4194cb51f393eefcf849fa93c72fe79fc792","reason":"The bounded artifact snapshot mechanism applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: Local exact-byte capture and per-file writing lack provenance authority, locking, crash durability, multi-file atomicity, and any external consequence claim. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Missing, aliased, nonordinary, oversized, empty, changed, or unwritable paths raise; prior per-file writes are not rolled back.","commit":"Capture commits only to an in-memory exact-byte Snapshot; materialization commits per file write and is not atomic across files, locked, fsynced, or crash durable.","finality":"Capture commits only to an in-memory exact-byte Snapshot; materialization commits per file write and is not atomic across files, locked, fsynced, or crash durable. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Missing, aliased, nonordinary, oversized, empty, changed, or unwritable paths raise; prior per-file writes are not rolled back."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8a3103e9bc3946e155f42077ba5f4194cb51f393eefcf849fa93c72fe79fc792","reason":"The bounded artifact snapshot mechanism applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: Local exact-byte capture and per-file writing lack provenance authority, locking, crash durability, multi-file atomicity, and any external consequence claim. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"No transaction identifier or duplicate ledger exists; retry re-reads current source bytes and can repeat or partially overwrite materialization effects.","idempotency":"The bounded artifact snapshot mechanism treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Inspect source and destination state, remove or reconcile only with separate authority, then explicitly recapture or rematerialize.","retry_limits":"No transaction identifier or duplicate ledger exists; retry re-reads current source bytes and can repeat or partially overwrite materialization effects."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:8a3103e9bc3946e155f42077ba5f4194cb51f393eefcf849fa93c72fe