bligation/check outcomes, blockers, certified depth, and output-write result only."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8897e9f0698600433657b217cf96a8794cbab79b040c1a00aa9db2e3a9b4b83","reason":"The certification command dispatcher applies as SENSOR. Its bounded software acquisition path has explicit source, range, latency, missingness, and fault behavior. Reviewed boundary: A selected certificate result does not by itself establish full object-profile conformance, application authority, checker confinement, publication, or release. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"The caller supplies selection and policy; certificate bytes cannot admit their own mechanism or grant owner, application, publication, human, legal, or release authority.","effects":"Run selected checks, aggregate bounded result rows, emit a status, and optionally create one certificate without overwriting an existing file.","preconditions":"A command mode, exact local records, independently selected request and policy, installed mechanisms, and optional new output path.","resources":"Selected local records, in-memory evidence/session state, registered mechanism code, standard output, and optional exclusive local certificate path."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8897e9f0698600433657b217cf96a8794cbab79b040c1a00aa9db2e3a9b4b83","reason":"The certification command dispatcher applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: A selected certificate result does not by itself establish full object-profile conformance, application authority, checker confinement, publication, or release. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Malformed selection, unsupported mechanism, missing evidence, checker exception, unavailable capacity, or write refusal remains rejected, FAIL, or UNKNOWN; partial effects are not erased.","commit":"Commit is a returned assessment/replay result and, when requested, one exclusive local certificate write; execution and output are not atomic together or crash durable.","finality":"Commit is a returned assessment/replay result and, when requested, one exclusive local certificate write; execution and output are not atomic together or crash durable. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed selection, unsupported mechanism, missing evidence, checker exception, unavailable capacity, or write refusal remains rejected, FAIL, or UNKNOWN; partial effects are not erased."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8897e9f0698600433657b217cf96a8794cbab79b040c1a00aa9db2e3a9b4b83","reason":"The certification command dispatcher applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: A selected certificate result does not by itself establish full object-profile conformance, application authority, checker confinement, publication, or release. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Retry repeats reads and mechanism execution; exclusive output refuses duplicates but checker side effects and prior emission are not rolled back.","idempotency":"The certification command dispatcher treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Inspect any optional output and mechanism-visible state, correct the independent inputs or installation, and explicitly start a fresh run.","retry_limits":"Retry repeats reads and mechanism execution; exclusive output refuses duplicates but checker side effects and prior emission are not rolled back."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e8897e9f0698600433657b217cf96a8794cbab79b040c1a00aa9db2e3a9b4b83","reason":"The certification command dispatcher applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded local read/write or evaluation attempt has explicit preconditions, commit evidence, partial-failure state, and retry semantics. Reviewed boundary: A selected certificate result does not by itself establish full object-profile conformance, application authority, checker confinement, publication, or release. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Selected input acquisition, built-in certification execution and exclusive local output creation."},"reason":"Checker invocation and output publication have authority, observation, effect and failure boundaries beyond passive verification metadata. Boundary: The command invokes no external domain mechanism and establishes no application-wide certification, sandboxing or endpoint authority.","specializations":["ACTUATOR","MEASUREMENT","POLICY","SENSOR","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:add_certification_parser","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:_read","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:handle_certification_command","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:_domain_command","python:src/verifier/runtime/certification_cli.py:_mainstay_command"]},{"classification":{"ACTOR":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f111612