urred even when its response is unavailable.","preconditions":"Exact endpoint, publisher/head coordinates, credential, object bytes, push manifest, claim bytes, and bounded expected response documents.","resources":"One exclusive local credential path and the explicitly selected Claim Garden registration, push, object, and claim endpoints."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2eeae4eff8ed693b3c87cb63f1a0bc37ca5e7ea1058dd130f21311e96dd98dd2","reason":"Claim Garden lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Pre-transport refusal is REJECTED; once a request may have reached the endpoint, an unavailable or inconsistent response remains INDETERMINATE or UNKNOWN and later phases are not assumed.","commit":"Commit is only the exact accepted response for the named phase, including stored digests and PENDING_REVIEW where required.","finality":"Commit is only the exact accepted response for the named phase, including stored digests and PENDING_REVIEW where required. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Pre-transport refusal is REJECTED; once a request may have reached the endpoint, an unavailable or inconsistent response remains INDETERMINATE or UNKNOWN and later phases are not assumed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2eeae4eff8ed693b3c87cb63f1a0bc37ca5e7ea1058dd130f21311e96dd98dd2","reason":"Claim Garden lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"The client performs no automatic retry after a transport attempt; exact content identities and server deduplication fields are checked where the protocol exposes them.","idempotency":"Claim Garden lifecycle treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Inspect the separately authenticated remote state before any manual retry; the client never treats a missing response as an abort or replays it automatically.","retry_limits":"The client performs no automatic retry after a transport attempt; exact content identities and server deduplication fields are checked where the protocol exposes them."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2eeae4eff8ed693b3c87cb63f1a0bc37ca5e7ea1058dd130f21311e96dd98dd2","reason":"Claim Garden lifecycle applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Compound Claim Garden publisher registration, object upload, push finalization and claim-publication transport."},"reason":"Authenticated multi-step remote exchanges have ordering, retry, partial-failure and finality semantics absent from generic ownership. Boundary: Path-level ownership cannot split the co-resident phases. Submission ends in bounded remote states and does not establish publication, moderation, real-money transfer or FINBOT responsibility.","specializations":["TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/interoperability/claim_garden.py","python:src/verifier/interoperability/claim_garden.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/interoperability/claim_garden.py:ClaimGardenClientError","python:src/verifier/inte