y; the session grants only one in-process callback admission and cannot confer downstream endpoint authority.","exceptions":"Configured active capacity and one-use identifiers bound admission.","revisions":"An RLock-protected session rechecks stop, capacity, and one-use invocation identity immediately before releasing the lock to call the callback."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:296ca934bc90124b9538a6038c527a29c8471be8d82b128a34e94ba0c9d18616","reason":"controlled emission session applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Configured active capacity and one-use identifiers bound admission.","decision_evidence":"The session observes its lock-protected state, active count, stop decision, callback return, and callback exception only.","enforcement_points":"An RLock-protected session rechecks stop, capacity, and one-use invocation identity immediately before releasing the lock to call the callback.","unavailable_behavior":"Stopped, duplicate, or over-capacity admission fails closed; unavailable stop/clock behavior remains UNKNOWN; active callbacks may continue."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:296ca934bc90124b9538a6038c527a29c8471be8d82b128a34e94ba0c9d18616","reason":"controlled emission session applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","roles":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","transitions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:296ca934bc90124b9538