pplies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Invalid selection and known refutation fail closed; missing applicability, unavailable mechanism or unestablished evidence remains UNKNOWN. Callback side effects and interruption cannot be rolled back here.","commit":"Commit is only retention or return of the typed core decision after its declared checks; callback return is not proof of downstream correctness.","finality":"Commit is only retention or return of the typed core decision after its declared checks; callback return is not proof of downstream correctness. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Invalid selection and known refutation fail closed; missing applicability, unavailable mechanism or unestablished evidence remains UNKNOWN. Callback side effects and interruption cannot be rolled back here."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:312a62657d3e3b8f9167af6fb90db7e7639a50d8434e28cc45a48d5625030401","reason":"core mechanism executor applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"No general callback idempotency or duplicate guard is assumed. A repeated evaluation is new execution and can repeat undeclared callback effects.","idempotency":"core mechanism executor treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Inspect external state after callback uncertainty, correct the exact selection or mechanism, and explicitly start a new evaluation; never infer that an exception erased callback effects.","retry_limits":"No general callback idempotency or duplicate guard is assumed. A repeated evaluation is new execution and can repeat undeclared callback effects."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:312a62657d3e3b8f9167af6fb90db7e7639a50d8434e28cc45a48d5625030401","reason":"core mechanism executor applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Core VERIFIER policy selection and execution of caller-registered in-process checking mechanisms."},"reason":"Admitted mechanism callbacks have authority, selection, limits and failure behavior that cannot remain implicit in generic VERIFIER ownership; callback replay does not itself establish an owned command-to-effect endpoint. Boundary: Trusted in-process callback execution is not a sandbox. A returned result proves neither absence of side effects nor external correctness; physical or financial endpoints separately accumulate ROBOT or FINBOT and every other applicable role.","specializations":["POLICY","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/core/certification_mechanisms.py","python:src/verifier/core/certification_mechanisms.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/core/certification_mechanisms.py:NativeCertificationMechanism","python:src/verifier/core/certification_mechanisms.py:NativeCertificationMechanism.mechanism_digest","python:src/verifier/core/certification_mechanisms.py:NativeCertificationMechanism.evaluate","file:src/verifier/core/depth.py","python:src/verifier/core/depth.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/