d registered native certificate replays, compare exact canonical outputs, and issue or reproduce the bounded CORE-SELF-POLISH receipt.","effect_domains":"LOCAL_FIXED_GIT_AND_INSTALLED_REPLAY_ONLY; the route reads source and executes installed compiler/checker code, but does not run arbitrary repository commands, publish, release, deploy, physically actuate, or transact money.","targets":"One selected Verifier source tree and worktree state, installed compiler/rule/route mechanisms, two selected Tier-1 objective certificates, and in-memory assessment and receipt values."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:3009b5e2dcc804613d49c15dad4a0902b7e9ab08ca12f9d7a4d9911c45f64c2b","reason":"core self-polish assessor applies as ACTUATOR. Its owned source connects an accepted command to a represented real or simulated effect endpoint and exposes effect feedback plus an explicit failure surface. Submission, dispatch, replay, callback entry, or child-process launch alone is insufficient. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.2-response-and-limits":{"declaration":{"limits":"Source files/bytes, Git outputs, selection/inventory/request/bundle bytes, objects, requirements, objectives, registered routes, compiler pins, and exact digest/shape checks are finite and fail closed.","response":"Git head/tree/index/status and source census, mechanism/source/instruction/rule digests, compiler and native replay status, installed counts, selected objective closure, recapture agreement, and receipt digest.","saturation":"Invalid or substituted selection/input FAILS; missing source/mechanism or cancellation remains UNKNOWN; resource exhaustion remains UNKNOWN; no partial replay or preparation alone issues a PASS receipt.","units_and_frames":"Exact bytes, source files, installed definitions/memberships, objects/requirements/objectives/certificates, fixed replay counts, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:3009b5e2dcc804613d49c15dad4a0902b7e9ab08ca12f9d7a4d9911c45f64c2b","reason":"core self-polish assessor applies as ACTUATOR. Its owned source connects an accepted command to a represented real or simulated effect endpoint and exposes effect feedback plus an explicit failure surface. Submission, dispatch, replay, callback entry, or child-process launch alone is insufficient. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.3-feedback-and-interlocks":{"declaration":{"effect_feedback":"Git head/tree/index/status and source census, mechanism/source/instruction/rule digests, compiler and native replay status, installed counts, selected objective closure, recapture agreement, and receipt digest.","failure_states":"Invalid or substituted selection/input FAILS; missing source/mechanism or cancellation remains UNKNOWN; resource exhaustion remains UNKNOWN; no partial replay or preparation alone issues a PASS receipt.","interlocks":"Source and mechanism capture precede preparation; external digest selection precedes assessment; source, compiler, object facets, typed facets, and native inventory replay must close in order; final recapture precedes receipt issue.","recovery":"Restore the exact externally selected source/mechanism/input set, prepare a new digest when anything changed, and rerun the full gate; never promote the narrow receipt to whole-application polish."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:3009b5e2dcc804613d49c15dad4a0902b7e9ab08ca12f9d7a4d9911c45f64c2b","reason":"core self-polish assessor applies as ACTUATOR. Its owned source connects an accepted command to a represented real or simulated effect endpoint and exposes effect feedback plus an explicit failure surface. Submission, dispatch, replay, callback entry, or child-process launch alone is insufficient. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfi