NT-0.1-phenomenon-and-method":{"declaration":{"method":"Capture Git/index/worktree and candidate-source census, bind installed mechanism sources and instructions, derive and reproduce structural compiler output, replay selected native objectives, recapture source, and issue/recheck a narrow receipt.","observation_vs_estimate":"core self-polish assessor reports only the parent-boundary observations named here. PASS covers only the exact CORE-SELF-POLISH-1 structural selection and two native Tier-1 replays. Full-application completeness, polished issuance, authority, public checkability, acceptance, release, ROBOT, and FINBOT consequences remain unestablished.","phenomenon":"Git head/tree/index/status and source census, mechanism/source/instruction/rule digests, compiler and native replay status, installed counts, selected objective closure, recapture agreement, and receipt digest.","source":"Exact source manifest and digest, application/object selections, source scope and collection bytes, compiler policy/manifest, polish request/bundle/inventory, selected certificates, expected digests, and optional cancellation callback."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:3009b5e2dcc804613d49c15dad4a0902b7e9ab08ca12f9d7a4d9911c45f64c2b","reason":"core self-polish assessor applies as MEASUREMENT. Its retained parent-boundary values distinguish what was observed from child or external state that was not observed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"core self-polish assessor records parent receipt/completion ordering; it does not reconstruct an unobserved child or external event time.","observation_time":"Fixed Git queries have finite timeouts and cancellation is observed at explicit stages; installed in-process compiler/checker calls have no general preemption or real-time guarantee.","reference_frame":"One selected Ve