n-process values and any files, processes, or endpoints explicitly selected by its owned sources."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f57ab11b21fcc1a4d3c17cf19d21a1a4031d08b493aa64ac5eb1806c6f0126f","reason":"vstd-data-receipt-lifecycle (GRAPH receipt construction, local artifact publication, validation, and reproduction lifecycle.) applies as ACTUATOR. Its owned source connects an accepted command to a represented real or simulated effect endpoint and exposes effect feedback plus an explicit failure surface. Submission, dispatch, replay, callback entry, or child-process launch alone is insufficient. Audited semantic basis: vstd-data-receipt-lifecycle owns GRAPH receipt construction, local artifact publication, validation, and reproduction lifecycle. Exact current source-byte denominator: src/verifier/data/receipt.py. Fixed operands: hardware=vstd-hardware, subject=vstd-data. Necessity: The receipt binds a data subject and hardware context while observing and mutating a selected local output directory under explicit policy. Consequence boundary: Publication is a non-atomic local multi-file write without external witness or durable truth; it proves neither source claims nor financial or physical effects. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed exact-source boundary only; mechanism execution, semantic truth, and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.2-response-and-limits":{"declaration":{"limits":"vstd-data-receipt-lifecycle declaration basis sha256:c0c4f63392308d96d853301be83eca8df288049ef34be29bb811530db8de49b1 binds exact source src/verifier/data/receipt.py; source role, necessity, consequence boundary, operands, and path set are hash-bound; declaration text alone establishes no execution truth. Field declaration: vstd-data-receipt-lifecycle (GRAPH receipt construction, local artifact publication, validation, and reproduction lifecycle.) is bounded by limits explicit in its exact source and declared role. Missing limits are not invented by thi