4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-measurement-vstd-dataset-provenance-policy-eb759a62c32e; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"ProvenanceHypergraph, target identifier, recorded statuses and rights, and optional approved license identifiers.","defaults":"No-revoked differs from all-valid; missing target and rootless license evidence are indeterminate. Missing rights do not satisfy approval; explicit empty license selection stays empty.","precedence":"Structural validity precedes decision. Grounded encoding is authoritative; solver/direct disagreements raise rather than choosing a preferred answer.","scope":"Three distinct predicates over the selected target's recorded ancestor closure, including the target itself."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d81fcd4f3e25c13ecd9c03283e486fa22441164069ec36b3842b9018fa170960","reason":"The installed provenance-policy engine decides three recorded-lineage predicates over status, rights, and approved source licenses; it establishes neither provenance truth nor legal or downstream enforcement authority. This source-bound Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"Each invocation reads its supplied graph and configuration; no cached approval or external enforcement activation is promised.","authority":"The caller selects the graph, predicate, and license list; authenticity of metadata and legal authority are outside this implementation.","exceptions":"No override argument bypasses structural or encoding checks; selecting a different predicate is a different named claim.","revisions":"Installed source defines each rule. Explicit per-call license selections replace that call's default list; there is no persistent revision service."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d81fcd4f3e25c13ecd9c03283e486fa22441164069ec36b3842b9018fa170960","reason":"The installed provenance-policy engine decides three recorded-lineage predicates over status, rights, and approved source licenses; it establishes neither provenance truth nor legal or downstream enforcement authority. This source-bound Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Malformed lineage and contradictory or incomplete encodings refuse; downstream callers remain responsible for enforcing these decisions.","decision_evidence":"Results carry policy and target identifiers, verdict, clauses, and variable map. Encoding errors may retain a kernel-checkable certificate; normal result records do not export it.","enforcement_points":"All three public verification methods validate structure and certify their emitted encoding before a determined result.","unavailable_behavior":"An absent target or rootless source-license question is INDETERMINATE, not successful compliance. Unsupported external truth is not inferred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d81fcd4f3e25c13ecd9c03283e486fa22441164069ec36b3842b9018fa170960","reason":"The installed provenance-policy engine decides three recorded-lineage predicates over status, rights, and approved source licenses; it establishes neither provenance truth nor legal or downstream enforcement authority. This source-bound Tier-0 declaration states the boundary; mechanism truth and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","roles":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","transitions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:3f104e027addeafafb181569009023864a079b9de2c9c6f95da5d113c89304b4","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-protocol-vstd-dataset-provenance-policy-3d3edc6df4bc; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","message_authority":