ess parser, installed handler, standard output, and process exit status only; handler-owned files and endpoints retain their separate object consequences."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:b0f9923e9edcedf35e76a6d5615186c315b86ea087d62c6fa9cece8bd9092e9a","reason":"The VSTD 3 hardware CLI protocol facade applies as TRANSACTION. Its optional local write or virtual receipt publication has explicit preconditions, commit, partial-failure, retry, and finality boundaries. Dispatch reaches hardware_probe_cli.py's save-then-validate receipt write and hardware_discovery_cli.py's optional --output write, so each reached handler's commit and partial-failure boundary is part of this facade's dispatch. Reviewed boundary: The facade is a software command protocol, not a sandbox, hardware sensor, physical controller, attestation root, durable ledger, or authority to publish or release. This Tier-0 declaration names only the exact reviewed source boundary; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Malformed values raise, unsupported or failed handlers retain their status, and output or handler exceptions abort the call without proving rollback of handler-owned effects.","commit":"Commit is the selected handler call plus emitted payload and returned exit code; there is no atomic cross-handler commit, durable history, or external finality.","finality":"Commit is the selected handler call plus emitted payload and returned exit code; there is no atomic cross-handler commit, durable history, or external finality. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed values raise, unsupported or failed handlers retain their status, and output or handler exceptions abort the call without proving rollback of handler-owned effects."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:b0f9923e9edcedf35e76a6d5615186c315b86ea087d62c6fa9cece8b