 and selected callback/certificate replay produce typed findings.","observation_vs_estimate":"native gate suite reports only the parent-boundary observations named here. This suite gives bounded local technical gate evidence only. It is not complete nine-tier or full-application polish, arbitrary command confinement, universal quality/safety, rights clearance, release authority, ROBOT, or FINBOT assurance.","phenomenon":"Selected byte digests, scan counts and violations, AST/pattern findings, Git/PRDEL and receipt results, applicability, checker statuses, execution observations, and closing source/manifest agreement.","source":"Exact target paths or snapshot bytes, bounded gate policy, selected manifest object/obligation, optional external request/policy/certificate evidence, source coordinate, and installed registry/mechanism bytes."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b41da8f2dbaf757e393e9cad27f392fe6cac1960af585fd2d90fc72b6bff220","reason":"native gate suite applies as MEASUREMENT. Its retained parent-boundary values distinguish what was observed from child or external state that was not observed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.2-units-time-and-uncertainty":{"declaration":{"arrival_time":"native gate suite records parent receipt/completion ordering; it does not reconstruct an unobserved child or external event time.","observation_time":"Individual fixed Git and selected checker routes carry their own finite limits; the suite provides no general callback preemption, real-time guarantee, or eventual closure.","reference_frame":"One declared local artifact snapshot or repository manifest object, installed gate implementations and native route callbacks, fixed Git queries, and in-memory clearance/gate reports.","uncertainty":"This suite gives bounded local technical gate evidence only. It is not complete nine-tier or full-application polish, arbitrary command confinement, universal quality/safety, rights clearance, release authority, ROBOT, or FINBOT assurance.","units":"Exact bytes, files/archive members/AST nodes/findings/gates, source lines, bounded iteration counts, process results, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b41da8f2dbaf757e393e9cad27f392fe6cac1960af585fd2d90fc72b6bff220","reason":"native gate suite applies as MEASUREMENT. Its retained parent-boundary values distinguish what was observed from child or external state that was not observed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MEASUREMENT-0.3-validity-and-missingness":{"declaration":{"freshness":"Individual fixed Git and selected checker routes carry their own finite limits; the suite provides no general callback preemption, real-time guarantee, or eventual closure.","missingness":"Detected contradictions FAIL; unsupported format, missing applicability/evidence, unavailable checker or incomplete scan remains UNKNOWN/UNSUPPORTED; source change invalidates acceptance.","provenance":"Bounded filesystem and archive reads, Python AST inspection, pattern matching, exact Git/PRDEL and receipt checks, installed gate discovery, source recapture, and selected callback/certificate replay produce typed findings.","validity":"File/archive/total bytes, path counts, AST traversal and static iteration bounds, policy terms/selections, supported contracts, evidence selections, and source recapture are finite and fail closed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4b41da8f2dbaf757e393e9cad27f392fe6cac1960af585fd2d90fc72b6bff220","reason":"native gate suite applies as MEASUREMENT. Its retained parent-boundary values distinguish what was observed from child or external state that was not observed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration"