r.","state":"Base, derived, composed, transferred, accepted-reference, intentionally invalid, rendered, written, and refused corpus states are explicitly represented."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:99094b46e68e6623129ab8b85c7b18cfa5dd97d693e41432a0f9f3a1538b5ba3","reason":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder applies as LEDGER. Its represented ordered records, invariants, replay, correction, and recovery boundary would be hidden by a generic fixture label. Exact source-specific basis: The corpus records ordered synthetic heads, commits, transfers, derivations, receipts, expected acceptance/rejection, and exact canonical digests. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.2-accounting-invariants":{"declaration":{"balance_rules":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder is an ordered event/accounting ledger, not a fungible balance sheet. Its invariant is the exact authorized and ordered commit contract: Commit is a complete bounded canonical fixture byte string written to the selected path; direct file writes are not crash-atomic or a multi-file transaction.","rounding":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder records exact discrete events and byte digests; it defines no numeric rounding convention or financial balance.","sources_and_sinks":"The scripts replace or create named local fixture files. Generated signed records model protocol and ledger effects but perform no live publication or transfer.","units":"Discrete synthetic records and cases, exact bytes and paths, sequence values, SHA-256 identities, and fixed test signatures; no monetary unit is represented."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:99094b46e68e6623129ab8b85c7b18cfa5dd97d693e41432a0f9f3a1538b5ba3","reason":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder applies as LEDGER. Its represented ordered records, invariants, replay, correction, and recovery boundary would be hidden by a generic fixture label. Exact source-specific basis: The corpus records ordered synthetic heads, commits, transfers, derivations, receipts, expected acceptance/rejection, and exact canonical digests. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder does not rewrite an accepted history entry; later action is a new ordered event or a separately retained recovery operation.","reconciliation":"The corpus records ordered synthetic heads, commits, transfers, derivations, receipts, expected acceptance/rejection, and exact canonical digests.","recovery":"Restore valid pinned inputs, inspect any output after write uncertainty, and regenerate deterministically; fixture regeneration does not repair live history.","replay":"Deterministic inputs should reproduce the same bytes; a retry may overwrite a prior output and does not reconcile a concurrent writer or partial filesystem effect."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:99094b46e68e6623129ab8b85c7b18cfa5dd97d693e41432a0f9f3a1538b5ba3","reason":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder applies as LEDGER. Its represented ordered records, invariants, replay, correction, and recovery boundary would be hidden by a generic fixture label. Exact source-specific basis: The corpus records ordered synthetic heads, commits, transfers, derivations, receipts, expected acceptance/rejection, and exact canonical digests. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.1-orders-and-access":{"declaration":{"cancellation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","order_states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","participant_access":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","validation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:630da27f4e0ceb50a8dcf767ef972fb0d643cc7efaae198d896d15c1e0f04bd7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-network-fixture-corpus-46a5c6c92a9e; fulfil