lment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"Missing or oversized source fixtures, malformed records, count/shape violations, encoding errors, or output I/O failures abort generation; a direct write can leave a partial or replaced file.","liveness":"Fixture timestamps are deterministic test data, not observations of occurrence time; builders provide no deadline, liveness, or real-network progress guarantee.","recovery":"Restore valid pinned inputs, inspect any output after write uncertainty, and regenerate deterministically; fixture regeneration does not repair live history.","safety":"Schemas, exact record fields, case counts, corpus byte caps, canonical ordering, digest/signature checks, and bounded source fixture reads constrain generation."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:99094b46e68e6623129ab8b85c7b18cfa5dd97d693e41432a0f9f3a1538b5ba3","reason":"The artifact-network fixture corpus builder applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants, ordered records or exchanges, compatibility, replay, failure, and progress semantics form a distinct protocol boundary. Exact source-specific basis: The local fixture builder, fixed synthetic publishers/signers, artifact-network record types, corpus consumers, selected source fixtures, and output paths. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:630da27f4e0ceb50a8dcf767ef972fb0d643cc7efaae198d896d15c1e0f04bd7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-network-fixture-corpus-a447eba23c30; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ES