ness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","missingness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","provenance":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","validity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-measurement-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-258dd4bf5073; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"POLICY-0.1-rules-and-precedence":{"declaration":{"decision_inputs":"Exact policy version, enforcement request with point, action, target and consequence roles, trust roots by authority, decision evidence, optional exceptions and current-revision pointer; for routes a fresh nonce and source pins.","defaults":"Malformed input, unverified authority, expired or revoked evidence, or an unmatched action yields REFUSED or UNAVAILABLE; worker failure or a mismatched nonce or pins yields UNKNOWN.","precedence":"Each enforce call appends one receipt after the previous digest; every consequence role is decided independently and must be allowed; the ledger is a new tuple per decision.","scope":"Evaluate one caller-supplied enforcement request against one versioned policy under verified decision authority and append exactly one hash-chained receipt; separately run fixed route cases in an isolated worker and judge its observations against an independent oracle."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:06f31e7d745679d1b39c399cb40fa5e7b781027b363d1176428359ae6132a16a","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"ALLOWED, REFUSED or UNAVAILABLE per decision, chained from a genesis digest; route status PASS, FAIL or UNKNOWN.","authority":"A decision needs a grant verified by a keyed hash under a caller-supplied trust root; the engine does not establish key custody, signer identity, or that a revision is published or current.","exceptions":"Closed field sets, finite enforcement points and consequence roles, bounded text and integers, and a bounded worker timeout.","revisions":"Closed-field policy, grant, exception, current-revision and request records; keyed HMAC authority over exact canonical policy digests; per-role evaluation by applicable rules with deny by default; UNAVAILABLE on any evaluation exception; a hash-chained receipt ledger; and a nonce and source-pin exchange with one fixed worker."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:06f31e7d745679d1b39c399cb40fa5e7b781027b363d1176428359ae6132a16a","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Closed field sets, finite enforcement points and consequence roles, bounded text and integers, and a bounded worker timeout.","decision_evidence":"Receipts with policy, request, authority, trust-root commitment and chain digests; bypass findings against recorded effects; worker observations with the echoed nonce and source pins.","enforcement_points":"Closed-field policy, grant, exception, current-revision and request records; keyed HMAC authority over exact canonical policy digests; per-role evaluation by applicable rules with deny by default; UNAVAILABLE on any evaluation exception; a hash-chained receipt ledger; and a nonce and source-pin exchange with one fixed worker.","unavailable_behavior":"Malformed input, unverified authority, expired or revoked evidence, or an unmatched action yields REFUSED or UNAVAILABLE; worker failure or a mismatched nonce or pins yields UNKNOWN."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:06f31e7d745679d1b39c399cb40fa5e7b781027b363d1176428359ae6132a16a","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"The caller, the enforcement engine, the decision authority named by a verified grant, and for route checks the parent evaluator and one fixed isolated worker.","roles":"Evaluate one caller-supplied enforcement request against one versioned policy under verified decision authority and append exactly one hash-chained receipt; separately run fixed route cases in an isolated worker and judge its observations against an independent oracle.","states":"ALLOWED, REFUSED or UNAVAILABLE per decision, chained from a genesis digest; route status PASS, FAIL or UNKNOWN.","transitions":"The parent sends one nonce request, the worker checks its own source pins before and after and echoes the nonce, and only an exact echo with matching pins lets the parent judge the worker's observations."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:58127961966b718ba1539903de670554a33ff2a1533ea406c1b6217f78972591","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants exchange ordered requests/responses across a process or remote boundary with explicit compatibility and failure states. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Closed-field policy, grant, exception, current-revision and request records; keyed HMAC authority over exact canonical policy digests; per-role evaluation by applicable rules with deny by default; UNAVAILABLE on any evaluation exception; a hash-chained receipt ledger; and a nonce and source-pin exchange with one fixed worker.","message_authority":"A decision needs a grant verified by a keyed hash under a caller-supplied trust root; the engine does not establish key custody, signer identity, or that a revision is published or current.","ordering":"Each enforce call appends one receipt after the previous digest; every consequence role is decided independently and must be allowed; the ledger is a new tuple per decision.","replay":"No automatic retry: an exception yields UNAVAILABLE, never ALLOWED, and the caller must issue a new request."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:58127961966b718ba1539903de670554a33ff2a1533ea406c1b6217f78972591","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants exchange ordered requests/responses across a process or remote boundary with explicit compatibility and failure states. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"Malformed input, unverified authority, expired or revoked evidence, or an unmatched action yields REFUSED or UNAVAILABLE; worker failure or a mismatched nonce or pins yields UNKNOWN.","liveness":"Policy and exception windows compare caller-supplied logical times; the worker call is bounded by a subprocess timeout, with no wall-clock freshness claim.","recovery":"Re-evaluate with corrected input; a broken chain or replay mismatch stays FAIL; decisions mutate no external state, so nothing is rolled back.","safety":"Closed field sets, finite enforcement points and consequence roles, bounded text and integers, and a bounded worker timeout."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:58127961966b718ba1539903de670554a33ff2a1533ea406c1b6217f78972591","reason":"policy enforcement engine applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants exchange ordered requests/responses across a process or remote boundary with explicit compatibility and failure states. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ROBOT-0.1-agent-to-actuator-binding":{"declaration":{"actuators":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","controllers":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-079051bc3ef8; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.2-physical-reach-and-observation":{"declaration":{"confinement_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","domain_crossings":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","observations":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","physical_reach":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-079051bc3ef8; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"ROBOT-0.3-consequences-and-intervention":{"declaration":{"hazards":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","intervention":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","safe_state_or_continuity":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-robot-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-079051bc3ef8; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.1-acquisition-and-observations":{"declaration":{"acquisition":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","deployment":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","measurements":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","phenomena":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-sensor-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-0b13aa6c10a2; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.2-calibration-and-envelope":{"declaration":{"calibration_applicability":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","calibration_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","drift":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","operating_range":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-sensor-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-0b13aa6c10a2; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"SENSOR-0.3-sampling-and-faults":{"declaration":{"fault_detection":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","latency":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","recovery":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","sampling":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-sensor-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-0b13aa6c10a2; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","effects":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","preconditions":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","resources":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-transaction-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-49002d92fe2b; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","commit":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","finality":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","partial_failure":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-transaction-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-49002d92fe2b; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","idempotency":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","replay":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","retry_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:2676ae155d21b14e23bf1ae6a4cebc9de80cf7e86592abc8ceab170d3c32d7f7","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-transaction-vstd-policy-enforcement-engine-49002d92fe2b; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Source-bound in-memory POLICY enforcement engine, its route cases and the isolated worker oracle that judges the engine's observations."},"reason":"enforce() decides each request under verified authority, exceptions, revisions, decision evidence and consequence roles and appends one hash-chained receipt per call, so the admission decision is POLICY. The route module starts the isolated worker and exchanges a nonce with source pins, and the worker runs the cases and judges them against an independent oracle, so the parent and worker exchange is PROTOCOL. Boundary: Decides caller-supplied requests in process and observes only calls made through enforce. It does not execute downstream effects, prove key custody or signer identity, establish publication or currentness of revisions, or establish the truth of the facts behind decision evidence. FINANCIAL and PHYSICAL roles are enforced as gates only, so no ACTUATOR, ROBOT or FINBOT role is accumulated. The worker is an isolated interpreter, not a filesystem, network or host sandbox, its fixture keys are not trust roots, and a route PASS is local field evidence, never route conformance.","specializations":["PROTOCOL"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:PolicyDefinitionError","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:PolicyBypassDetected","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:PolicyBypassDetected.__init__","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_closed","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_text","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_integer","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_flag","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_texts","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_sign","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_verify","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:_file_digest","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:Rule","python:src/verifier/runtime/policy_enforcement_execution.py:Rule.__post_init__","python:src/verif