nputs as refusal or UNKNOWN rather than silently inferring success.","precedence":"vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy declaration basis sha256:7917132fb24c18d317efd7819f8787e6298969e803f70074558deb01c63473b8 binds exact source .gitattributes, .gitignore, MANIFEST.in; source role, necessity, consequence boundary, operands, and path set are hash-bound; declaration text alone establishes no execution truth. Field declaration: vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy (Repository text-normalization, ignored-path and source-distribution inclusion declarations.) uses only order explicitly represented by its source-defined calls, records, or dependencies; no global temporal order is inferred.","scope":"vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy declaration basis sha256:7917132fb24c18d317efd7819f8787e6298969e803f70074558deb01c63473b8 binds exact source .gitattributes, .gitignore, MANIFEST.in; source role, necessity, consequence boundary, operands, and path set are hash-bound; declaration text alone establishes no execution truth. Field declaration: vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy (Repository text-normalization, ignored-path and source-distribution inclusion declarations.) is reviewed only as the path-owned source role declared by the audited partition. Its exact source denominator is .gitattributes, .gitignore, MANIFEST.in."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:e9d4ee2dce583a1b82d3c0fad02dd62fcb2c69f7fd86d64194fc103548a14e4a","reason":"vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy (Repository text-normalization, ignored-path and source-distribution inclusion declarations.) applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. Audited semantic basis: vstd-repository-file-and-package-policy owns Repository text-normalization, ignored-path and source-distribution inclusion declarations. Exact current source-byte denominator: .gitattributes, .gitignore, MANIFEST.in. Fixed operands: none. Necessity: G