trusted root capability. Acceptance grants bounded local reads only and does not establish content correctness, repository completeness, or release authority.","commands":"Bind the admitted root, duplicate/inspect/close handles, open one declared member relative to that root, read bounded bytes, and load the selected scope.","feedback":"The mechanism observes manifest identity, root volume/file identity, path and handle metadata snapshots, cancellation state, exact member bytes, sizes, and SHA-256 correspondence.","objectives":"Admit one externally bound repository root and read only the regular members named by its exact manifest, source coordinate, generation, and byte bounds."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as CONTROLLER. It selects and sequences consequential acquisition, checking, replay, or output commands using bounded feedback and stop states. Exact source-specific basis: Admit one externally bound repository root and read only the regular members named by its exact manifest, source coordinate, generation, and byte bounds. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.2-timing-and-stability":{"declaration":{"operating_envelope":"Canonical path components, regular-file and no-reparse rules, generation and root identity, per-member and total bytes, declared sizes/digests, and exact source coordinate fail closed.","saturation":"Malformed, stale, reused, mismatched, escaped, linked, nonregular, oversized, changed, cancelled, unreadable, or incompletely cleaned inputs fail closed; cleanup uncertainty is retained rather than hidden.","stability_assumptions":"The selected-source admission mechanism controls a bounded software lifecycle, not a proved dynamical plant; safe downstream stability remains outside this Tier-0 claim.","timing":"Cancellation is chec