ier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.2-calibration-and-envelope":{"declaration":{"calibration_applicability":"Physical calibration is not applicable to The selected-source admission mechanism's digital parent-interface acquisition; parser and source pins are compatibility bindings, not metrological calibration.","calibration_evidence":"Strict manifest parsing, SHA-256 and size checks, canonical relative paths, Windows handle-relative no-follow traversal, before/open/after identity snapshots, cancellation checks, and deterministic handle cleanup.","drift":"Cancellation is checked at traversal and read boundaries, but there is no deadline, freshness age, atomic repository snapshot, or real-time guarantee.","operating_range":"Canonical path components, regular-file and no-reparse rules, generation and root identity, per-member and total bytes, declared sizes/digests, and exact source coordinate fail closed."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as SENSOR. It actively acquires those digital observations and therefore needs an explicit source, range, drift, latency, and fault boundary. Exact source-specific basis: Strict manifest parsing, SHA-256 and size checks, canonical relative paths, Windows handle-relative no-follow traversal, before/open/after identity snapshots, cancellation checks, and deterministic handle cleanup. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"SENSOR-0.3-sampling-and-faults":{"declaration":{"fault_detection":"Malformed, stale, reused, mismatched, escaped, linked, nonregular, oversized, changed, cancelled, unreadable, or incompletely cleaned inputs fail closed; cleanup uncertainty is retained rather than hidden.","latency":"Cancellation is checked at traversal and read boundaries, but there is no deadline, freshness age, atomic repository snapshot, or real-time guarantee.","recovery":"Correct the external admission, manifest, handle, source materialization, bounds, or cancellation condition and begin a new admission/read; never infer that a failed or cancelled read spent or rolled back external state.","sampling":"The mechanism observes manifest identity, root volume/file identity, path and handle metadata snapshots, cancellation state, exact member bytes, sizes, and SHA-256 correspondence."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as SENSOR. It actively acquires those digital observations and therefore needs an explicit source, range, drift, latency, and fault boundary. Exact source-specific basis: Strict manifest parsing, SHA-256 and size checks, canonical relative paths, Windows handle-relative no-follow traversal, before/open/after identity snapshots, cancellation checks, and deterministic handle cleanup. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.1-effects-and-authority":{"declaration":{"authorization":"The caller must supply both the external admission record and trusted root capability. Acceptance grants bounded local reads only and does not establish content correctness, repository completeness, or release authority.","effects":"A successful bind adds one admission id to the caller-owned set; reads open and close local handles and return exact bytes without writing member content.","preconditions":"Exact manifest bytes and digest, source and materialization coordinates, root volume/file identity, current generation, admission id, byte bounds, trusted handle, and optional cancellation predicate.","resources":"The caller-owned consumed-admission set, borrowed root capability, duplicated handles, and exact manifest-listed regular files under the selected root."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded state or file effect has preconditions, commit, partial-failure, retry, and replay consequences that must be explicit. Exact source-specific basis: A successful bind adds one admission id to the caller-owned set; reads open and close local handles and return exact bytes without writing member content. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Malformed, stale, reused, mismatched, escaped, linked, nonregular, oversized, changed, cancelled, unreadable, or incompletely cleaned inputs fail closed; cleanup uncertainty is retained rather than hidden.","commit":"Binding commits only after all admission and root checks, when the id is added and the bounded view is returned. Each member read commits only as a checked observation; this is not package-wide repository admission.","finality":"Binding commits only after all admission and root checks, when the id is added and the bounded view is returned. Each member read commits only as a checked observation; this is not package-wide repository admission. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed, stale, reused, mismatched, escaped, linked, nonregular, oversized, changed, cancelled, unreadable, or incompletely cleaned inputs fail closed; cleanup uncertainty is retained rather than hidden."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded state or file effect has preconditions, commit, partial-failure, retry, and replay consequences that must be explicit. Exact source-specific basis: A successful bind adds one admission id to the caller-owned set; reads open and close local handles and return exact bytes without writing member content. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"A consumed admission id is refused. Failed pre-commit binding leaves the set unchanged; a repeated member read is a fresh observation and may see drift.","idempotency":"The selected-source admission mechanism treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Correct the external admission, manifest, handle, source materialization, bounds, or cancellation condition and begin a new admission/read; never infer that a failed or cancelled read spent or rolled back external state.","retry_limits":"A consumed admission id is refused. Failed pre-commit binding leaves the set unchanged; a repeated member read is a fresh observation and may see drift."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9cec2d0ad3cf0afb86e1eb0d63717071b0868234ea5a1568a11b4fdfae7ca676","reason":"The selected-source admission mechanism applies as TRANSACTION. Its bounded state or file effect has preconditions, commit, partial-failure, retry, and replay consequences that must be explicit. Exact source-specific basis: A successful bind adds one admission id to the caller-owned set; reads open and close local handles and return exact bytes without writing member content. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Externally authorized source-member admission, anchored acquisition, cancellation and single-use commit tools."},"reason":"Selected source admission observes exact identity and bytes, applies caller-provided policy and commits one bounded handle, so control, observation, protocol and transaction roles are necessary. Boundary: Admission covers only the supplied manifest, handle and selected members; it does not establish repository completeness, authorship, semantic correctness, release admissibility, durable replay, sandboxing, physical effect or financial effect.","specializations":["CONTROLLER","MEASUREMENT","PROTOCOL","SENSOR","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:<module>","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootError","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:RootAdmission","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_ByHandleFileInformation","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_reject","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_is_bounded_int","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_is_sha256","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_validate_root_handle","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_validate_admission","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_borrowed_root_identity","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_duplicate_root_handle","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_close_duplicated_root_handle","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_materialization_coordinate","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:_check_observation","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootBinding","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootBinding.__init__","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootBinding.admitted_paths","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootBinding.read_member","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:AdmittedRootBinding.load_scope","python:scripts/admitted_root_binding.py:bind_admitted_root","file:scripts/exact_materialized_member.py","python:scripts/exact_materialized_member.py:<module>","python:scripts/exact_materialized_member.py:MaterializedMemberError","python:scripts/exact_materialized_member.py:MaterializedMem