ord after its declared checks. It is not an atomic external commit, tier PASS, application qualification, release, or deployment.","finality":"Commit is only return of the named bounded in-process record after its declared checks. It is not an atomic external commit, tier PASS, application qualification, release, or deployment. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed selection or native contradiction fails; unavailable execution remains UNKNOWN unless failure was already observed; partial PASS is never promoted."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9197726bad5aad119a77f7ea7a4e99ec7b10b5f56da5266996aceb4a8753c2ae","reason":"The source-native Dynamics controller applies as TRANSACTION. Its selected execution attempt has explicit preconditions, named effects, commit evidence, partial failure, finality, and retry boundaries. Reviewed boundary: The fixed progression is not an application certificate DAG, historical resource attestation, whole-tier proof, host truth, or external effect authority. Audited source anchor: self_polish_dynamics.py:170-174,205-225. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Each call is a new evaluation of its selected inputs and current source. No retained result, duplicate identity, rollback, or general idempotency is inferred.","idempotency":"The source-native Dynamics controller treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Retain the failure or UNKNOWN boundary, correct the exact input or source condition, and explicitly start a fresh evaluation; never upgrade an earlier or partial result.","retry_limits":"Each call is a new evaluation of its selected inputs and current source. No retained result, duplicate identity, rollback, or general idempotency is inferred."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9197726bad5aad119a77f7ea7a4e99ec7b10b5f56da5266996aceb4a8753c2ae","reason":"The source-native Dynamics controller applies as TRANSACTION. Its selected execution attempt has explicit preconditions, named effects, commit evidence, partial failure, finality, and retry boundaries. Reviewed boundary: The fixed progression is not an application certificate DAG, historical resource attestation, whole-tier proof, host truth, or external effect authority. Audited source anchor: self_polish_dynamics.py:170-174,205-225. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Fresh cumulative Tier-1 and Tier-2 triad replay, including process-backed fresh SIM variants."},"reason":"Progression acquires current source and replay outcomes, commands selected rechecks, and gates later states through bounded manifest and receipt exchanges. Boundary: The fixed installed route union is not arbitrary-application completeness, a historical resource claim, physical control or financial authority.","specializations":["ACTUATOR","CONTROLLER","MEASUREMENT","POLICY","PROTOCOL","SENSOR","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:mechanism_digest","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:_join","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:_replay","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:_reasons","python:src/verifier/runtime/self_polish_dynamics.py:assess_native_dynamics"]},{"classification":{"ACTOR":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"ACTUATOR":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256: