ompression overflow, duplicate entries, count mismatch, digest mismatch, or invalid case shape is rejected before data is returned.","precedence":"Capacity and encoding checks precede decode; exact registry identity and duplicate checks precede return of the case mapping.","scope":"Source-owned positive, negative, and unavailable specimen inputs, adapter selections, and expected outcomes for installed native routes."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:cd9c8ede2890515404650c77832ba5f1fc34051b05948168eff85b55e4439e19","reason":"The installed native case registry applies as POLICY. Its denominator, selection rules, authority boundary, precedence, defaults, exceptions, and enforcement points decide the bounded result. Reviewed boundary: Decoding and registration perform no replay and establish no route, tier, package, release, deployment, host, physical, or financial conformance. Audited source anchor: self_polish_native_cases.py:2992-3042; self_polish_native_tier3_cases.py:1877-1913. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.2-authority-and-exceptions":{"declaration":{"activation":"Embedded, decoded, registry-bound, returned as policy data, malformed, oversized, count-different, or digest-different.","authority":"The installed source defines case-admission policy only; registration cannot authorize replay, qualify a route, or promote a tier.","exceptions":"Fixed per-module entry counts and digests, bounded encoded/compressed/decompressed bytes, unique keys, and explicit triad labels are required.","revisions":"Boundedly decode embedded canonical case payloads, check fixed entry counts and registry digests, and return immutable input records; no builder or rechecker is invoked."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:cd9c8ede2890515404650c77832ba5f1fc34051b05948168eff85b55e4439e19","reason":"The installed native case registry applies as POLICY. Its denominator, selection rules, authority boundary, precedence, defaults, exceptions, and enforcement points decide the bounded result. Reviewed boundary: Decoding and registration perform no replay and establish no route, tier, package, release, deployment, host, physical, or financial conformance. Audited source anchor: self_polish_native_cases.py:2992-3042; self_polish_native_tier3_cases.py:1877-1913. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"POLICY-0.3-enforcement-and-decisions":{"declaration":{"bypass_handling":"Fixed per-module entry counts and digests, bounded encoded/compressed/decompressed bytes, unique keys, and explicit triad labels are required.","decision_evidence":"Encoded/compressed/decompressed sizes, entry identity and count, registry digest, adapter selection, input payload, and expected outcome labels.","enforcement_points":"Boundedly decode embedded canonical case payloads, check fixed entry counts and registry digests, and return immutable input records; no builder or rechecker is invoked.","unavailable_behavior":"Malformed encoding, decompression overflow, duplicate entries, count mismatch, digest mismatch, or invalid case shape is rejected before data is returned."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:cd9c8ede2890515404650c77832ba5f1fc34051b05948168eff85b55e4439e19","reason":"The installed native case registry applies as POLICY. Its denominator, selection rules, authority boundary, precedence, defaults, exceptions, and enforcement points decide the bounded result. Reviewed boundary: Decoding and registration perform no replay and establish no route, tier, package, release, deployment, host, physical, or financial conformance. Audited source anchor: self_polish_native_cases.py:2992-3042; self_polish_native_tier3_cases.py:1877-1913. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"d