an atomic external commit, tier PASS, application qualification, release, or deployment.","rounding":"The source-derived Tier-Zero reason ledger records exact discrete events and byte digests; it defines no numeric rounding convention or financial balance.","sources_and_sinks":"Read current mechanism bytes and return a deterministic reason ledger and receipt; execute no route certificate and change no repository state.","units":"Exact bytes, SHA-256 digests, finite route/candidate/obligation counts, ordered records, and explicit PASS, FAIL, UNKNOWN, or lifecycle labels."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:58870da122b03f6b32b52b699f9095c461f8f10728ca8bcc2ed1d2fee0d0d364","reason":"The source-derived Tier-Zero reason ledger applies as LEDGER. Its authoritative ordered reason denominator, identity, correction, replay, and recovery semantics cannot be reduced to generic data. Reviewed boundary: Annotation binding proves neither an annotation's semantic claim nor any route, slot, repository, tier, application, release, or deployment fulfillment. Audited source anchor: tier_zero_reasons.py:185-226. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"The source-derived Tier-Zero reason ledger does not rewrite an accepted history entry; later action is a new ordered event or a separately retained recovery operation.","reconciliation":"Route and slot identity, rationale, checking-mechanism path and digest, semantic digest, evidence requirements, preserved/unpreserved semantics, residuals, falsifiers, and counts.","recovery":"Retain the failure or UNKNOWN boundary, correct the exact input or source condition, and explicitly start a fresh evaluation; never upgrade an earlier or partial result.","replay":"Each call is a new evaluation of its selected inputs and current source. No retained result, duplicate identity, rollback, or general i