dden by a generic fixture label. Exact source-specific basis: It observes current Git repository/revision, file digests, pytest collection results, legacy inventory/mapping correspondence, replay receipt structure, and local writes.","status":"APPLIES"},"MARKET":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"MEASUREMENT":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:5fb0c05c02df8aa1a1f4c84024b45695a7327d5315a1a34900f85de8d638e12b","reason":"The legacy Tier-1 evidence ledger builder applies as MEASUREMENT. It captures host or repository values, so direct observations must be distinguished from inferred completeness and semantic truth. Exact source-specific basis: It observes current Git repository/revision, file digests, pytest collection results, legacy inventory/mapping correspondence, replay receipt structure, and local writes.","status":"APPLIES"},"MODEL":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"OWNER":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"POLICY":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:5fb0c05c02df8aa1a1f4c84024b45695a7327d5315a1a34900f85de8d638e12b","reason":"The legacy Tier-1 evidence ledger builder applies as POLICY. Its admission or case-selection rules, precedence, defaults, exceptions, and enforcement decide what may be accepted or emitted. Exact source-specific basis: Build and optionally replay an external FACETS evidence template for the pinned legacy inventory of 26 object kinds, 45 Tier-1 memberships, and 135 mapped cases.","status":"APPLIES"},"PROTOCOL":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:5fb0c05c02df8aa1a1f4c84024b45695a7327d5315a1a34900f85de8d638e12b","reason":"The legacy Tier-1 evidence ledger builder applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants, ordered records or exchanges, compatibility, replay, failure, and progress semantics form a distinct protocol boundary. Exact source-specific basis: The local caller, legacy installed-route inventory, source/test files, Git and pytest child processes, evidence/replay records, and selected output paths.","status":"APPLIES"},"RECEIPT":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"ROBOT":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"ROLE":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"SENSOR":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:5fb0c05c02df8aa1a1f4c84024b45695a7327d5315a1a34900f85de8d638e12b","reason":"The legacy Tier-1 evidence ledger builder applies as SENSOR. It actively acquires those digital observations and therefore needs an explicit source, range, drift, latency, and fault boundary. Exact source-specific basis: The script validates pinned inventory identities and source mappings, acquires Git coordinates and file digests, launches bounded pytest collection, builds UNKNOWN ledger entries, validates replay receipts, and writes selected JSON artifacts.","status":"APPLIES"},"SIM":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"SPACE":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"TIME":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"TOKEN":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","reason":"UNRESOLVED.","status":"UNRESOLVED"},"TRAIN":{"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:4f53cda18c2baa0c