 binding mutation, activation, launch, fork, delegation, model/evaluator change, or checkpoint write only when the selected plan permits it.","feedback":"Current authority generation/digest, clock, local stop/revocation/use state, callback return/exception, and retained EVENT chain.","objectives":"Mediate one authenticated TRAIN action against exact plan, policy, current capability, stop, attribution, target, and bounded session-event state."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as CONTROLLER. Its state, feedback, admission decisions, commands, timing, and intervention behavior form a bounded software control loop. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.2-timing-and-stability":{"declaration":{"operating_envelope":"Finite keys, principals, scopes, evidence bytes, events, status age, invocation ceilings, and exact plan targets.","saturation":"Malformed/refuted authority fails; unavailable clock/provider/backend remains UNKNOWN; STOP prevents new admission but not active preemption.","stability_assumptions":"TRAIN control session controls a bounded software lifecycle, not a proved dynamical plant; safe downstream stability remains outside this Tier-0 claim.","timing":"Trusted clock freshness and grant windows are rechecked at the final boundary; active callbacks are not preempted."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as CONTROLLER. Its state, feedback, admission decisions, commands, timing, and intervention behavior form a bounded software control loop. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.3-intervention-and-failure":{"declaration":{"arbitration":"All authority/stop/replay checks and reservation occur under the lock before one callback runs outside it and completion is recorded.","failure_behavior":"Use a new root-authorized session/current authority view; retained denial replay proves only its bounded historical predicate.","feedback_loss":"Malformed/refuted authority fails; unavailable clock/provider/backend remains UNKNOWN; STOP prevents new admission but not active preemption.","intervention":"Latch authenticated STOP or submit one exact protected TRAIN action callback, including binding mutation, activation, launch, fork, delegation, model/evaluator change, or checkpoint write only when the selected plan permits it."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as CONTROLLER. Its state, feedback, admission decisions, commands, timing, and intervention behavior form a bounded software control loop. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"FINBOT-0.1-agent-and-financial-authority":{"declaration":{"agent":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","decision_scope":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","financial_authority":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","harness":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-finbot-vstd-train-control-session-df5cf95991ae; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"FINBOT-0.2-financial-exposure-and-dependencies":{"declaration":{"assets_and_parties":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","exposure_limits":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","financial_dependencies":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","real_world_paths":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-finbot-vstd-train-control-session-df5cf95991ae; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"FINBOT-0.3-decisions-effects-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"decision_effect_evidence":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","intervention":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","limit_enforcement":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","reconciliation_and_recovery":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-finbot-vstd-train-control-session-df5cf95991ae; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"LEDGER-0.1-authoritative-history":{"declaration":{"authority":"Configured host root/executor keys and current native TOKEN grants authorize the exact operation; MODEL-origin proposals are denied.","history":"Current authority generation/digest, clock, local stop/revocation/use state, callback return/exception, and retained EVENT chain.","ordering":"All authority/stop/replay checks and reservation occur under the lock before one callback runs outside it and completion is recorded.","state":"Preflight, admitted, active, stopped, spent, revoked/suspended, PASS, FAIL, UNKNOWN, and retained-event states."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as LEDGER. Its locally authoritative ordered history and recovery behavior would be hidden by a generic object label. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.2-accounting-invariants":{"declaration":{"balance_rules":"TRAIN control session is an ordered event/accounting ledger, not a fungible balance sheet. Its invariant is the exact authorized and ordered commit contract: Commit means the host callback returned or raised and the session attempted to retain its completion EVENT; retention is not guaranteed when the plan context cannot be resolved, and downstream checkpoint/training truth is not established.","rounding":"TRAIN control session records exact discrete events and byte digests; it defines no numeric rounding convention or financial balance.","sources_and_sinks":"Spend one request/capability use, call the host effect once, and append one bounded local EVENT outcome.","units":"Discrete capability uses/events, integer trusted-clock observations, exact bytes, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as LEDGER. Its locally authoritative ordered history and recovery behavior would be hidden by a generic object label. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"LEDGER-0.3-correction-and-recovery":{"declaration":{"corrections":"TRAIN control session does not rewrite an accepted history entry; later action is a new ordered event or a separately retained recovery operation.","reconciliation":"Current authority generation/digest, clock, local stop/revocation/use state, callback return/exception, and retained EVENT chain.","recovery":"Use a new root-authorized session/current authority view; retained denial replay proves only its bounded historical predicate.","replay":"Request identifiers and capability invocation ceilings prevent replay; callback uncertainty is not automatically retried."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as LEDGER. Its locally authoritative ordered history and recovery behavior would be hidden by a generic object label. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"MARKET-0.1-orders-and-access":{"declaration":{"cancellation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","order_states":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","participant_access":"NOT_ESTABLISHED","validation":"NOT_ESTABLISHED"},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"reasons.vstd:tier0-market-vstd-train-control-session-7abc28e4a6ac; fulfillment NOT_ESTABLISHED."},"MARKET-0.2-matching-and-allo