ot active preemption.","commit":"Commit means the host callback returned or raised and the session attempted to retain its completion EVENT; retention is not guaranteed when the plan context cannot be resolved, and downstream checkpoint/training truth is not established.","finality":"Commit means the host callback returned or raised and the session attempted to retain its completion EVENT; retention is not guaranteed when the plan context cannot be resolved, and downstream checkpoint/training truth is not established. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Malformed/refuted authority fails; unavailable clock/provider/backend remains UNKNOWN; STOP prevents new admission but not active preemption."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"Request identifiers and capability invocation ceilings prevent replay; callback uncertainty is not automatically retried.","idempotency":"TRAIN control session treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Use a new root-authorized session/current authority view; retained denial replay proves only its bounded historical predicate.","retry_limits":"Request identifiers and capability invocation ceilings prevent replay; callback uncertainty is not automatically retried."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:7c33b5a3b0a9b4c9c097c6aa2b1d839d006dba8e2a502253c9a7e79079d326bd","reason":"TRAIN control session applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Authenticated TRAIN action mediation, stop policy and bounded session event control."},"reason":"Training changes require explicit authority, timing, replay and intervention behavior rather than generic TRAIN ownership. Its lock-protected hash-linked EVENT chain is the locally authoritative bounded history used for capacity, admission and denial replay, so the LEDGER role remains explicit even though the history is not durable. Boundary: Action or callback submission is not proof of downstream effect. The local EVENT ledger has no restart durability or reconciliation path and can omit an outcome when plan context cannot be resolved. Trusted-host mediation is not a sandbox; actual physical or financial endpoints accumulate ROBOT or FINBOT and their other applicable roles.","specializations":["LEDGER","POLICY","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:_plain","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:_plain.visit","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:operation_signing_bytes","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:operation_scope","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:TrainControlPolicy","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:TrainControlPolicy.__post_init__","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:TrainControlPolicy.digest","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:AuthoritySnapshot","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:MediatedResult","python:src/verifier/corrigibility/train_control.py:_C