tion tags over canonical request bodies, precondition snapshots, operation identity with replay detection, bounded retry, injected-crash checkpoints, idempotent compensation, and state derived fresh from the journal and observed resource values.","unavailable_behavior":"An invalid form is refused without partial mutation; a simulated crash at a checkpoint leaves a journal from which state is derived; divergence is reported, not hidden."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as POLICY. Its rule selection, authority, defaults, and enforcement points decide whether a consequential operation may proceed. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.1-participants-and-states":{"declaration":{"participants":"The caller, one coordinator, two in-memory resources, and a named authorizer whose key is held in process.","roles":"Run one declared two-resource transaction through prepare, commit, abort and compensate over in-memory resources with a hash-chained journal, and reconcile intended against applied effects.","states":"Prepared, committed, aborted, compensated or refused, with committed, aborted and compensated terminal; every state is derived from the journal, never stored.","transitions":"Phases follow the closed prepare, commit, abort and compensate state machine, and a replayed operation identity returns its recorded receipt."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants exchange ordered requests/responses across a process or remote boundary with explicit compatibility and failure states. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.2-ordering-and-replay":{"declaration":{"compatibility":"Closed request and receipt schemas, keyed authorization tags over canonical request bodies, precondition snapshots, operation identity with replay detection, bounded retry, injected-crash checkpoints, idempotent compensation, and state derived fresh from the journal and observed resource values.","message_authority":"A keyed tag from a named authorizer over the canonical request body; the key registry is in process, so real authorizer identity is not established.","ordering":"Journal entries are append-only and hash-chained from a genesis digest, and phases follow prepare, then commit, abort or compensate.","replay":"A declared bounded retry limit; a replayed operation identity returns its recorded outcome and is not applied twice."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as PROTOCOL. Its participants exchange ordered requests/responses across a process or remote boundary with explicit compatibility and failure states. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"PROTOCOL-0.3-failures-and-progress":{"declaration":{"failure_assumptions":"An invalid form is refused without partial mutation; a simulated crash at a checkpoint leaves a journal from which state is derived; divergence is reported, not hidden.","liveness":"Phases are deterministic and ordered by the journal; no wall-clock timing, deadline or concurrency claim is made.","recovery":"Compensation is idempotent and reconcile reports intended against applied effects; durability across process loss is NOT_ESTABLISHED.","safety":"A fixed maximum number of effects and retries, two named resources, and closed field sets."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as P