applied and recorded in the journal; a refused form leaves the resources unchanged.","finality":"Commit is the boundary at which all declared effects are applied and recorded in the journal; a refused form leaves the resources unchanged. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"An invalid form is refused without partial mutation; a simulated crash at a checkpoint leaves a journal from which state is derived; divergence is reported, not hidden."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"A declared bounded retry limit; a replayed operation identity returns its recorded outcome and is not applied twice.","idempotency":"in-memory transaction coordinator treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"Compensation is idempotent and reconcile reports intended against applied effects; durability across process loss is NOT_ESTABLISHED.","retry_limits":"A declared bounded retry limit; a replayed operation identity returns its recorded outcome and is not applied twice."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:d543b6414fed1b0caf3ef507439844afb5f6e57358a711859ad988dd9840b376","reason":"in-memory transaction coordinator applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Deterministic in-memory two-resource transaction coordinator with a hash-chained journal."},"reason":"Prepare, commit, abort, compensate and reconcile are state transitions over an append-only journal with retry and compensation rules, which is TRANSACTION. The closed phase and replay state machine is PROTOCOL, and the keyed authorization over canonical request bodies with precondition gating is POLICY. Boundary: Mutates only in-memory LocalResource dictionaries. Precondition snapshot binding, keyed authorization, replay and bounded retry are established inside this model only. Durability, concurrent writers, external settlement, external atomicity, real authorizer identity and any finality beyond the local final record are NOT_ESTABLISHED, and the coordinator performs no external actuation.","specializations":["POLICY","PROTOCOL"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:SimulatedCrash","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_Injected","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_Refused","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_Refused.__init__","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_canonical","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_digest","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_same","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_scalar","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_text","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_safe_id","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_closed","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_retry","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_rows","python:src/verifier/runtime/transaction_execution.py:_semantic","python:src/ve