applied Job limits, current membership and retained-handle signals, lifetime counts, output size, completion/timeout, exit code, exact reply bytes, and proof/work fields.","saturation":"Unsupported platforms or unavailable enforcement remain UNKNOWN; malformed or contradictory proof replies FAIL; timeout, output exhaustion, incomplete cleanup, or changed source never becomes PASS.","units_and_frames":"Committed bytes, output bytes, wall seconds, dimensionless process and proof counts, charged work units, and SHA-256 identities."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db3e5a22b2799bf37ff9b6ea3b1a68711982cc94a422624fa59b49e6d202481d","reason":"native VERIFIER execution controller applies as ACTUATOR. Its owned source connects an accepted command to a represented real or simulated effect endpoint and exposes effect feedback plus an explicit failure surface. Submission, dispatch, replay, callback entry, or child-process launch alone is insufficient. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"ACTUATOR-0.3-feedback-and-interlocks":{"declaration":{"effect_feedback":"The parent observes applied Job limits, current membership and retained-handle signals, lifetime counts, output size, completion/timeout, exit code, exact reply bytes, and proof/work fields.","failure_states":"Unsupported platforms or unavailable enforcement remain UNKNOWN; malformed or contradictory proof replies FAIL; timeout, output exhaustion, incomplete cleanup, or changed source never becomes PASS.","interlocks":"Request validation and complete work reservation precede child creation; job assignment and exact limit verification precede resume; completion observation precedes reply acceptance; termination and handle cleanup are mandatory.","recovery":"The parent terminates the exact owned Job, waits for retained handles, closes all handles, discards the uncertain reply, and requires a separate fresh run after the unavailable co