"TRANSACTION-0.2-commit-and-failure":{"declaration":{"abort":"Unsupported platforms or unavailable enforcement remain UNKNOWN; malformed or contradictory proof replies FAIL; timeout, output exhaustion, incomplete cleanup, or changed source never becomes PASS.","commit":"Commit is only a validated PASS reply whose request, checker, toolchain, proof digest, work use, pre-resume limits, and observed empty-job cleanup all match.","finality":"Commit is only a validated PASS reply whose request, checker, toolchain, proof digest, work use, pre-resume limits, and observed empty-job cleanup all match. This finality is limited to the named local or remote state; it grants no broader correctness or publication authority.","partial_failure":"Unsupported platforms or unavailable enforcement remain UNKNOWN; malformed or contradictory proof replies FAIL; timeout, output exhaustion, incomplete cleanup, or changed source never becomes PASS."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db3e5a22b2799bf37ff9b6ea3b1a68711982cc94a422624fa59b49e6d202481d","reason":"native VERIFIER execution controller applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"TRANSACTION-0.3-retry-and-replay":{"declaration":{"duplicate_detection":"No automatic proof retry occurs. Membership disagreement receives at most four bounded observations; any later invocation is a new process execution with a new observation boundary.","idempotency":"native VERIFIER execution controller treats only the explicitly named digest, request, or invocation identity as duplicate evidence; no unstated idempotency is assumed.","replay":"The parent terminates the exact owned Job, waits for retained handles, closes all handles, discards the uncertain reply, and requires a separate fresh run after the unavailable condition is corrected.","retry_limits":"No automatic proof retry occurs. Membership disagreement receives at most four bounded observations; any later invocation is a new process execution with a new observation boundary."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:db3e5a22b2799bf37ff9b6ea3b1a68711982cc94a422624fa59b49e6d202481d","reason":"native VERIFIER execution controller applies as TRANSACTION. Its named changes, response-dependent finality, duplicate handling, and partial-failure state require an explicit transaction boundary. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."}},"operands":{},"payload":{"representation_role":"Bounded native child-process launch, Windows Job control, resource observation and limit evaluation."},"reason":"Launching and terminating a process from observed resource feedback is an effectful verification controller, not a passive VERIFIER declaration. Boundary: The fixed parent-child exchange and host counters are not a sandbox, hostile-host attestation, semantic correctness proof, physical controller, ROBOT endpoint or financial authority.","specializations":["ACTUATOR","CONTROLLER","MEASUREMENT","POLICY","PROTOCOL","SENSOR","TRANSACTION"],"surfaces":["file:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:<module>","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_supported_platform","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_checker_digest","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob.__init__","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob.__init__.Basic","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob.__init__.Extended","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob.__init__.Accounting","python:src/verifier/domains/verifier_execution.py:_WindowsJob.__init__.ProcessIds","python:s