hed."},"CONTROLLER-0.2-timing-and-stability":{"declaration":{"operating_envelope":"One evidence bundle, at most thirty-two constraints and sixty-four declarations, bounded canonical bytes/items/operations/events, supported registered routes, and no nested VERIFIER-3.1/4.1 replay.","saturation":"Malformed/substituted inputs, exceeded declared maxima, refusal, or differing reports FAIL; unsupported quantities, exhausted checker ceiling, displaced trace, or unavailable child remain UNKNOWN.","stability_assumptions":"VERIFIER run-constraint controller controls a bounded software lifecycle, not a proved dynamical plant; safe downstream stability remains outside this Tier-0 claim.","timing":"No wall-time or external scheduling observation is made. Trace-event exhaustion bounds only counted CPython events during each selected in-process replay."},"evidence_set_digest":"sha256:9739662be589fdd2a5bf34693898be27b9d78354b7f0b0a0e9c53356c97a8341","reason":"VERIFIER run-constraint controller applies as CONTROLLER. Its state, feedback, admission decisions, commands, timing, and intervention behavior form a bounded software control loop. This Tier-0 declaration names the reviewed boundary only; mechanism execution and Tier-1-plus fulfillment remain unestablished."},"CONTROLLER-0.3-intervention-and-failure":{"declaration":{"arbitration":"Policy and all digest bindings are validated before replay; nesting is refused; two sequential traced replays must produce identical canonical reports; observed constraints are then compared before certificate construction.","failure_behavior":"Restore the previous trace hook unconditionally, correct the exact selected request/policy/certificate or ceiling, and start a new assessment; caller observations cannot fill a missing checker observation.","feedback_loss":"Malformed/substituted inputs, exceeded declared maxima, refusal, or differing reports FAIL; unsupported quantities, exhausted checker ceiling, displaced trace, or unavailable child remain 